// 写作 · 模拟题（按四级真题标准自编，明确标注为模拟题，不是真题）
// 题数：80 道（8 个主题，每主题 10 道）。
// 主题：教育、科技、环境、健康、社会现象、文化、校园生活、职业规划。
// 数据来源：英语四级学习页 artifact（ying-yu-si-ji-xue-xi）的 exportWritingMock 动作分批返回（start=0/count=50 + start=50/count=50），原样返回。
// 内容未改写：每道带主题、题型、标题、Directions 原文、参考范文（120–180 词）、逐句解析（好词/好句/好结构标注）、字数要求 120–180 词、建议时间 30 分钟。
// 科技主题第 4 道（tech-m4，大学生沉迷手机）是之前备好的写作第 4 题草稿，范文 147 词，原样收进来了，source 标注为“模拟题（原备好的写作第 4 题草稿）”。
// 格式：window.ENG_WRITING_MOCK = [{ id, kind, themeId, themeName, type, title, prompt, essay: [段落], analysis: [{en, note, tag}], wordRequirement, suggestedMinutes, source }]
window.ENG_WRITING_MOCK = [{"analysis":[{"en":"Nowadays, some people argue that a college degree is no longer a ticket to success, pointing to famous businessmen who never finished university.","note":"先摆出对方观点，pointing to… 用分词短语补充论据，一句话把背景说清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my opinion, however, a degree remains important for most young people.","note":"第一段就明确表态，however 一转，立场干净利落——观点类最忌模棱两可。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, a degree is often the basic requirement for a good job.","note":"理由段主题句先行，后面再展开，阅卷人一眼看到层次。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Most companies use it to judge whether an applicant has the knowledge and the ability to learn.","note":"applicant（求职者）是教育求职话题的准词；whether 引导宾语从句显得正式。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, university education gives students far more than a certificate.","note":"far more than（远不止）一句点出第二个理由的核心，比再列一条更凝练。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"During four years of study, they develop critical thinking, communication skills and a broad view of the world, all of which will benefit them for life.","note":"三个并列名词排比 + all of which 非限定性定语从句收尾，是全篇的亮点句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Admittedly, a degree alone cannot guarantee success, and personal effort matters as well.","note":"Admittedly 让步：先承认对方有道理，文章显得客观、不极端。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"But without the training behind the degree, many doors would never open at all.","note":"without 虚拟条件 + doors open 的比喻，把让步又拉回自己的立场。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, although success depends on many factors, a college degree is still a valuable starting point for most people today.","note":"结尾 although 让步从句 + 重申观点，和首段呼应，全文闭环。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Nowadays, some people argue that a college degree is no longer a ticket to success, pointing to famous businessmen who never finished university. In my opinion, however, a degree remains important for most young people.","First, a degree is often the basic requirement for a good job. Most companies use it to judge whether an applicant has the knowledge and the ability to learn. Second, university education gives students far more than a certificate. During four years of study, they develop critical thinking, communication skills and a broad view of the world, all of which will benefit them for life. Admittedly, a degree alone cannot guarantee success, and personal effort matters as well. But without the training behind the degree, many doors would never open at all.","In conclusion, although success depends on many factors, a college degree is still a valuable starting point for most people today."],"id":"edu-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people argue that a college degree is no longer necessary for success. What is your opinion? Write an essay of 120–180 words expressing your view.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"大学文凭对成功是否必要","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"People often debate whether book knowledge or practical experience matters more.","note":"一句摆出争议双方，观点类经典起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, the two cannot be separated, but if I have to choose, I believe practical experience plays a slightly more important role.","note":"先讲辩证再表态，slightly（稍微）留有分寸，不把话说满。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There is no doubt that books are a treasure house of knowledge.","note":"There is no doubt that… + treasure house（宝库）比喻，先扬书本。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Through reading, we can learn in a few days what others spent years discovering, and theory gives us a map before we start.","note":"what 宾语从句 + map 比喻，把书本的价值说得具体形象。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, knowledge that is never used soon fades.","note":"短句转折，定语从句压缩信息，转折干脆有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A medical student may recite every page of a textbook, yet only in the hospital does he learn how to face a real patient.","note":"举例 + only in…does he… 倒装，全篇最亮的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Experience turns dead knowledge into living ability, and it also tests and corrects what books tell us.","note":"dead / living 一对反义词对比；turn…into… 句型好用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, books light the way, but experience teaches us how to walk.","note":"比喻对仗收尾，呼应前文的 map，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The wisest choice is to learn from both, with experience as the final teacher.","note":"最高级 wisest 点题，with 短语收束，全文落点清楚。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["People often debate whether book knowledge or practical experience matters more. In my view, the two cannot be separated, but if I have to choose, I believe practical experience plays a slightly more important role.","There is no doubt that books are a treasure house of knowledge. Through reading, we can learn in a few days what others spent years discovering, and theory gives us a map before we start. However, knowledge that is never used soon fades. A medical student may recite every page of a textbook, yet only in the hospital does he learn how to face a real patient. Experience turns dead knowledge into living ability, and it also tests and corrects what books tell us.","In conclusion, books light the way, but experience teaches us how to walk. The wisest choice is to learn from both, with experience as the final teacher."],"id":"edu-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people believe that knowledge from books is more important, while others value practical experience more. Which do you think is more important? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"书本知识与实践经验哪个更重要","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"On campus today, a common scene is that students bury themselves in past exam papers while showing little interest in the knowledge itself.","note":"用一个具体场景开头，bury themselves in（埋头于）形象生动，比空喊 nowadays 好。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Exam preparation has replaced real learning for many students, and this phenomenon deserves our attention.","note":"第二句点明现象本质 + deserves our attention 引出下文分析，现象类标准起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Several factors contribute to this situation.","note":"原因段总起句，contribute to 是「导致、促成」的高分搭配。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, scores are still the main standard by which students are judged.","note":"by which 定语从句把「评判标准」说得正式准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Scholarships, job offers and further study all depend heavily on grades, so students naturally aim at high marks instead of deep understanding.","note":"三个名词并列举例说明分数的重要性；aim at、instead of 对比清楚。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In addition, many exams test memory rather than ability.","note":"rather than（而不是）是分析类作文的核心对比词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When memorizing model answers can bring a good score, few students are willing to spend extra time exploring a subject.","note":"when 从句 + 逻辑推论，把「考试方式决定学习方式」讲透。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Finally, heavy course loads leave students little time to learn at their own pace.","note":"at their own pace（按自己的节奏）是地道搭配；leave sb little time 句型好用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, exams should be a tool to check learning, not the purpose of learning itself.","note":"not…but 的变体对比收尾观点，一句话立意拔高。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Only when students learn for knowledge rather than for scores can education play its true role.","note":"Only when…can… 倒装结尾，全篇最有力的一句，值得背下来套用。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["On campus today, a common scene is that students bury themselves in past exam papers while showing little interest in the knowledge itself. Exam preparation has replaced real learning for many students, and this phenomenon deserves our attention.","Several factors contribute to this situation. To begin with, scores are still the main standard by which students are judged. Scholarships, job offers and further study all depend heavily on grades, so students naturally aim at high marks instead of deep understanding. In addition, many exams test memory rather than ability. When memorizing model answers can bring a good score, few students are willing to spend extra time exploring a subject. Finally, heavy course loads leave students little time to learn at their own pace.","In my view, exams should be a tool to check learning, not the purpose of learning itself. Only when students learn for knowledge rather than for scores can education play its true role."],"id":"edu-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many students spend most of their time preparing for exams rather than truly learning. Analyze the causes of this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"只备考、不真学","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In recent years, online courses have become a common way of learning for college students.","note":"In recent years + 现在完成时，利弊类最稳的开头。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Like most new things, this way of learning has both advantages and disadvantages.","note":"一句预告全文结构：下面就要分两面写。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, online learning is flexible and convenient.","note":"On the one hand / On the other hand 是利弊类的骨架词，必须成对出现。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students can study wherever they are and whenever they like, and they can watch a difficult part again and again until they fully understand it.","note":"wherever/whenever 让步状语从句 + again and again，把「灵活、可重复」写具体了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It also saves the time and money spent on the way to the classroom.","note":"spent on… 过去分词作后置定语，句子立刻紧凑起来。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On the other hand, online learning requires strong self-discipline.","note":"self-discipline（自律）是这个话题的关键词，写对了就显水平。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Without a teacher present, some students are easily distracted by games and social media.","note":"without 短语作条件，be distracted by（被……分心）搭配准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, staring at a screen for long hours does harm to the eyes and reduces face-to-face communication with teachers and classmates.","note":"do harm to（对……有害）、face-to-face 都是可直接迁移的高频搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, the advantages of online learning outweigh its disadvantages if it is used properly.","note":"outweigh 是利弊类结尾神词，记住：advantages outweigh disadvantages，不加 than。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It should serve as a helpful supplement to, rather than a complete replacement of, the traditional classroom.","note":"supplement（补充）与 replacement（替代）对比定位，rather than 夹在中间，判断有分寸。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In recent years, online courses have become a common way of learning for college students. Like most new things, this way of learning has both advantages and disadvantages.","On the one hand, online learning is flexible and convenient. Students can study wherever they are and whenever they like, and they can watch a difficult part again and again until they fully understand it. It also saves the time and money spent on the way to the classroom. On the other hand, online learning requires strong self-discipline. Without a teacher present, some students are easily distracted by games and social media. Besides, staring at a screen for long hours does harm to the eyes and reduces face-to-face communication with teachers and classmates.","In conclusion, the advantages of online learning outweigh its disadvantages if it is used properly. It should serve as a helpful supplement to, rather than a complete replacement of, the traditional classroom."],"id":"edu-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Online courses are becoming increasingly popular among college students. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of online learning and give your own conclusion in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"在线课程与传统课堂","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"For many freshmen, the first term at university is harder than they expected.","note":"一句话锁定人群和问题，问题解决型的开头不要绕。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used to being pushed by teachers in high school, they suddenly find that nobody tells them what to do, and some begin to fall behind.","note":"Used to… 分词短语作状语交代原因，fall behind（落后）是校园话题准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The problems are clear.","note":"短句单独成段感，起承上启下作用，阅卷读起来不累。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Without fixed homework and frequent tests, many students waste a lot of time and only start to review before exams.","note":"without 短语点出「没人管」的具体表现，问题写得具体才有分。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Others keep using high-school methods, memorizing everything by heart, which does not work for college courses that require understanding and independent thinking.","note":"by heart（背诵）地道；which 非限定从句补充评价；independent thinking 是教育主题核心词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To solve these problems, freshmen should first learn to make their own study plans and stick to them, for example by reviewing each week's lessons every Friday.","note":"To solve these problems 直接进入对策段；建议带 for example 的具体做法，不空喊。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Besides, they should make good use of resources around them: the library, office hours and senior students can all offer great help.","note":"make good use of（充分利用）替换 use well；冒号后列举资源，信息密度高。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In a word, the key is to change from passive learning to active learning as early as possible.","note":"passive → active 一组反义对比点题，In a word 收尾干净。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["For many freshmen, the first term at university is harder than they expected. Used to being pushed by teachers in high school, they suddenly find that nobody tells them what to do, and some begin to fall behind.","The problems are clear. Without fixed homework and frequent tests, many students waste a lot of time and only start to review before exams. Others keep using high-school methods, memorizing everything by heart, which does not work for college courses that require understanding and independent thinking.","To solve these problems, freshmen should first learn to make their own study plans and stick to them, for example by reviewing each week's lessons every Friday. Besides, they should make good use of resources around them: the library, office hours and senior students can all offer great help. In a word, the key is to change from passive learning to active learning as early as possible."],"id":"edu-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many freshmen find it hard to get used to the way of learning at university. What problems do they face, and how can they solve them? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"新生跟不上大学的学习节奏","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Li Hua,","note":"书信格式第一项：称呼 + 逗号，格式分先拿稳。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am glad to hear that you are going to start your university life soon.","note":"回信开头先回应对方近况，建议信的礼貌起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"You asked me how to learn English well in college, and I would like to share some advice that worked for me.","note":"一句点明写信目的；advice that worked for me（对我管用的建议）显得真诚可信。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"First of all, make English a part of your daily life.","note":"建议分点用 First of all / Second / Finally，建议信主体就靠这三个词撑起来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Spend at least half an hour every day on listening and reading, because language learning depends on steady accumulation rather than last-minute effort.","note":"建议具体到「每天半小时」；steady accumulation（稳步积累）与 last-minute effort（临时抱佛脚）对比，是全篇亮点。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, do not be afraid of making mistakes.","note":"祈使句给建议，简洁有力；be afraid of making mistakes 搭配准确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Join the English corner and speak as much as possible; only by opening your mouth can you truly improve.","note":"only by…can you… 倒装，把「开口说」这个建议说得有分量。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Finally, set clear goals, such as passing CET-4 in the first year, so that you always know what you are working for.","note":"such as 举例 + so that 目的从句，建议落到可执行的点上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I hope these suggestions will be helpful to you.","note":"结尾祝愿句，建议信的固定收尾，别省。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am sure you will make great progress if you keep going.","note":"再补一句鼓励：keep going（坚持下去），书信结尾有温度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Yours sincerely,","note":"书信结尾敬语 + 署名 Li Ming——题目要求不用真名，写错署名直接扣格式分。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Li Hua,","I am glad to hear that you are going to start your university life soon. You asked me how to learn English well in college, and I would like to share some advice that worked for me.","First of all, make English a part of your daily life. Spend at least half an hour every day on listening and reading, because language learning depends on steady accumulation rather than last-minute effort. Second, do not be afraid of making mistakes. Join the English corner and speak as much as possible; only by opening your mouth can you truly improve. Finally, set clear goals, such as passing CET-4 in the first year, so that you always know what you are working for.","I hope these suggestions will be helpful to you. I am sure you will make great progress if you keep going.","Yours sincerely,","Li Ming"],"id":"edu-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Your junior schoolmate Li Hua is about to enter university and asks you for advice on how to learn English well in college. Write him a letter of advice in 120–180 words. Do not sign your own name; use “Li Ming” instead.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"建议信：怎样学好英语","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Many universities now require students to take some courses outside their major, and this practice has caused heated discussion.","note":"cause heated discussion（引发热议）是观点类万能背景句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"As far as I am concerned, it is a good idea and benefits students in the long run.","note":"As far as I am concerned 表态 + in the long run（从长远看），立场明确又留余地。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, knowledge from other fields broadens students' horizons.","note":"broaden one's horizons（开阔眼界）是教育主题必备词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A computer science student who studies psychology, for example, may design products that understand users better.","note":"举例不空说：具体到「计算机学生学心理学」，例子越具体越有说服力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Moreover, modern problems are rarely solved by one subject alone.","note":"rarely 半否定句，第二条理由一句话立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Environmental protection needs science, law and economics at the same time, so students with wide knowledge are better prepared for future challenges.","note":"三个学科并列举例；be prepared for（为……做好准备）搭配地道。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Admittedly, courses outside the major take time and may add pressure.","note":"Admittedly 让步，先认下对方的担忧。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, universities can solve this by offering interesting choices and limiting the number of required courses.","note":"让步之后马上给出解决办法，文章不止于表态，还有建设性。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In short, learning beyond one's major is not a waste of time.","note":"In short 收尾重申，用否定句回应质疑。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It helps students grow into the kind of talent that society really needs.","note":"grow into（成长为）结尾升华，把话题落到「社会需要的人才」。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Many universities now require students to take some courses outside their major, and this practice has caused heated discussion. As far as I am concerned, it is a good idea and benefits students in the long run.","To begin with, knowledge from other fields broadens students' horizons. A computer science student who studies psychology, for example, may design products that understand users better. Moreover, modern problems are rarely solved by one subject alone. Environmental protection needs science, law and economics at the same time, so students with wide knowledge are better prepared for future challenges. Admittedly, courses outside the major take time and may add pressure. However, universities can solve this by offering interesting choices and limiting the number of required courses.","In short, learning beyond one's major is not a waste of time. It helps students grow into the kind of talent that society really needs."],"id":"edu-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some universities require students to take courses outside their major. Do you think this requirement is a good idea? Write 120–180 words to state your view.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"要不要修专业之外的课","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In recent years, studying abroad has become a popular choice for Chinese students.","note":"现象类标准开头：一句话点出现象。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Statistics show that hundreds of thousands of students go overseas for education every year, and the number is still growing.","note":"Statistics show that… 引出数据支撑；数据不必真实，但格式要像真的、量级要合理。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There are several reasons for this trend.","note":"trend（趋势）替换 phenomenon 避免重复；总起句开启原因段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, foreign universities offer high-quality education and advanced research facilities, which attract students who want a better academic environment.","note":"facilities（设施）、academic environment 都是教育话题准词；which 从句接得自然。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, an overseas experience can broaden students' horizons and improve their language skills, making them more competitive in the job market.","note":"making them… 分词短语补结果；competitive in the job market（在就业市场有竞争力）实用搭配。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In addition, as Chinese families become wealthier, more parents can afford the cost of sending their children abroad.","note":"as 引导原因背景；afford the cost of（负担得起……的费用）写对了显功底。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my opinion, studying abroad is a valuable opportunity, but it is not the only road to success.","note":"评论部分先肯定再限定，不走极端。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students should make the decision based on their own goals and conditions, instead of blindly following others.","note":"based on、blindly follow（盲目跟风）收尾，建议具体且切题。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["In recent years, studying abroad has become a popular choice for Chinese students. Statistics show that hundreds of thousands of students go overseas for education every year, and the number is still growing.","There are several reasons for this trend. First, foreign universities offer high-quality education and advanced research facilities, which attract students who want a better academic environment. Second, an overseas experience can broaden students' horizons and improve their language skills, making them more competitive in the job market. In addition, as Chinese families become wealthier, more parents can afford the cost of sending their children abroad.","In my opinion, studying abroad is a valuable opportunity, but it is not the only road to success. Students should make the decision based on their own goals and conditions, instead of blindly following others."],"id":"edu-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: In recent years, an increasing number of Chinese students choose to study abroad. Analyze the reasons behind this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"留学热","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"When it comes to learning, students have different habits: some prefer to study in groups, while others enjoy studying alone.","note":"When it comes to… 引出话题；some…while others… 一句摆出两方，对比类开头范式。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Both ways have their own strengths, and the choice depends on the task and the person.","note":"先不定论，预告下文要分两面讲，结构感强。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Studying in groups is efficient in many ways.","note":"动名词作主语开启第一面，主题句先行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Members can share materials, explain difficult points to each other and keep each other motivated.","note":"三个动词并列，好处列得具体；keep sb motivated（让某人保持动力）地道。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When one student gets stuck on a problem, a different idea from a partner often lights the way.","note":"get stuck on（被卡住）口语化准词；lights the way 比喻收尾，生动。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, group study can easily turn into group chatting, and its pace may not suit everyone.","note":"turn into group chatting 一个细节把缺点写活了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Studying alone, by contrast, allows students to concentrate fully and arrange their time freely.","note":"by contrast（相比之下）切换到第二面；allow sb to do 句型稳。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The weakness is that without discussion, some misunderstandings may stay hidden for a long time.","note":"表语从句指出独学的隐患，分析有来有回。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"As for me, I prefer group study for difficult subjects and studying alone before exams.","note":"个人选择不搞一刀切：分情况表态，显得成熟。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used in the right situation, both ways can serve us well.","note":"分词短语开头收尾，一句话总结两面，干净。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["When it comes to learning, students have different habits: some prefer to study in groups, while others enjoy studying alone. Both ways have their own strengths, and the choice depends on the task and the person.","Studying in groups is efficient in many ways. Members can share materials, explain difficult points to each other and keep each other motivated. When one student gets stuck on a problem, a different idea from a partner often lights the way. However, group study can easily turn into group chatting, and its pace may not suit everyone. Studying alone, by contrast, allows students to concentrate fully and arrange their time freely. The weakness is that without discussion, some misunderstandings may stay hidden for a long time.","As for me, I prefer group study for difficult subjects and studying alone before exams. Used in the right situation, both ways can serve us well."],"id":"edu-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some students prefer to study in groups, while others like to study alone. Compare the two ways of learning and state which one you prefer in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"小组学习与独自学习","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Heavy academic pressure has become a common problem among college students.","note":"问题解决型开头：一句点明问题，不铺垫。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many of them feel anxious about exams, assignments and their future, and some even suffer from poor sleep because of it.","note":"feel anxious about、suffer from 把压力的后果写具体，问题才显得值得解决。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The pressure mainly comes from two sources.","note":"总起句预告两个来源，段落骨架先立住。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, courses at university are more difficult and the competition is fiercer than in high school; a small slip may mean a much lower ranking.","note":"分号连接因果，a small slip（一点失误）说法形象。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On the other hand, students set high expectations for themselves.","note":"set high expectations for oneself（对自己期望高）是准搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"They want good grades, scholarships and a bright future all at once, so they never allow themselves to relax.","note":"all at once（全都同时要）把「自我加压」写透了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To deal with the pressure, students should first learn to plan their time and break big tasks into small steps, which makes them less frightening.","note":"对策段开头 To deal with…；break big tasks into small steps 是可执行的具体建议。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Besides, regular exercise and talking to friends or teachers can effectively relieve stress.","note":"relieve stress（缓解压力）固定搭配；两条建议并在一个句子里。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"After all, pressure in itself is not a bad thing; the key is to keep it at a healthy level.","note":"After all 收尾升华：辩证看压力，比单纯喊「放松」高一层。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Heavy academic pressure has become a common problem among college students. Many of them feel anxious about exams, assignments and their future, and some even suffer from poor sleep because of it.","The pressure mainly comes from two sources. On the one hand, courses at university are more difficult and the competition is fiercer than in high school; a small slip may mean a much lower ranking. On the other hand, students set high expectations for themselves. They want good grades, scholarships and a bright future all at once, so they never allow themselves to relax.","To deal with the pressure, students should first learn to plan their time and break big tasks into small steps, which makes them less frightening. Besides, regular exercise and talking to friends or teachers can effectively relieve stress. After all, pressure in itself is not a bad thing; the key is to keep it at a healthy level."],"id":"edu-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many college students are under heavy pressure from their studies. What causes the pressure, and what can students do to deal with it? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"education","themeName":"教育","title":"大学生的学业压力","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"With the development of artificial intelligence, AI tools have entered the classroom and become study partners for many students.","note":"With the development of… 是科技题的标准开头；study partners 把 AI 拟人化，生动。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Their influence on learning is a topic worth discussing.","note":"短句收尾第一段，worth discussing 点出「值得讨论」，自然引出利弊。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, AI tools can greatly improve learning efficiency.","note":"利弊类骨架词 On the one hand 先行，主题句明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They answer questions at any time of the day, explain difficult points in simple words and help students check their writing within seconds.","note":"三个动词并列把好处列具体；within seconds 强调速度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For shy students who dare not ask teachers, such tools are especially helpful.","note":"举出具体人群（害羞的学生），好处不空泛。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On the other hand, depending too much on AI may weaken students' own thinking.","note":"On the other hand 与前面成对；depending too much on 是弊端的核心说法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If every essay is polished by a machine and every problem is solved by an app, students gradually lose the ability to think independently.","note":"if 条件句 + every…every… 排比，把「依赖」的后果推到极端来讲清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There is also the risk that AI sometimes provides wrong information with great confidence.","note":"There is the risk that… 是提出隐患的正式句式；with great confidence 一笔写出 AI 出错的特点。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, AI tools should be used as assistants, not substitutes.","note":"assistants, not substitutes——对仗定位，科技题万能结论句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Only when students think first and use AI to check and improve can technology truly serve learning.","note":"Only when…can… 倒装收尾，落点在「先自己想」，立场有分寸。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["With the development of artificial intelligence, AI tools have entered the classroom and become study partners for many students. Their influence on learning is a topic worth discussing.","On the one hand, AI tools can greatly improve learning efficiency. They answer questions at any time of the day, explain difficult points in simple words and help students check their writing within seconds. For shy students who dare not ask teachers, such tools are especially helpful. On the other hand, depending too much on AI may weaken students' own thinking. If every essay is polished by a machine and every problem is solved by an app, students gradually lose the ability to think independently. There is also the risk that AI sometimes provides wrong information with great confidence.","In my view, AI tools should be used as assistants, not substitutes. Only when students think first and use AI to check and improve can technology truly serve learning."],"id":"tech-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: More and more students use artificial intelligence tools to help with their study. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this practice and give your conclusion in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"用 AI 工具辅助学习","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"It is often said that modern technology is making people lazy.","note":"It is often said that… 引出题目观点，观点类常用起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Washing machines wash our clothes, apps deliver our meals, and search engines answer our questions.","note":"三个排比短句举例，节奏感强，画面一下就出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, however, technology does not make people lazy; it simply changes where our effort goes.","note":"反驳式表态：不是变懒，是努力换了地方——立意新颖是观点类高分关键。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In the past, people spent most of their energy on physical work that machines now do better and faster.","note":"定语从句把今昔对比压缩进一句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Freed from such work, we can devote our time to more creative and valuable tasks, such as learning new skills and solving complex problems.","note":"Freed from… 分词开头；devote time to（把时间投入到）准搭配。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Those who seem lazy with technology were probably lazy without it; a diligent student uses a dictionary app to learn more words, while a lazy one uses the same app to copy homework.","note":"全文最亮的一句：同一个人、同一个 App，勤惰对比，论证一击命中。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The tool is the same, but the attitude is different.","note":"短句总结对比，干净有力，适合背下来当过渡句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, laziness is a choice of the person, not a product of technology.","note":"结尾重申立场，not… 对比收束。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Blaming machines for our own habits is itself a kind of laziness in thinking.","note":"最后一句反将一军：怪机器本身就是思维懒惰——结尾有余味。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["It is often said that modern technology is making people lazy. Washing machines wash our clothes, apps deliver our meals, and search engines answer our questions. In my view, however, technology does not make people lazy; it simply changes where our effort goes.","In the past, people spent most of their energy on physical work that machines now do better and faster. Freed from such work, we can devote our time to more creative and valuable tasks, such as learning new skills and solving complex problems. Those who seem lazy with technology were probably lazy without it; a diligent student uses a dictionary app to learn more words, while a lazy one uses the same app to copy homework. The tool is the same, but the attitude is different.","In conclusion, laziness is a choice of the person, not a product of technology. Blaming machines for our own habits is itself a kind of laziness in thinking."],"id":"tech-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people say that modern technology is making people lazier and lazier. Do you agree or disagree? Write 120–180 words to support your view.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"科技是否让人变懒","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Modern technology surrounds us in almost every part of life, yet people hold different views on whether it has made life simpler or more complicated.","note":"一句摆出现象 + whether 从句摆出争议，观点类开头一气呵成。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Personally, I believe technology has made life simpler in most ways, though it does bring new troubles.","note":"表态带 though 让步，不把话说满，显得客观。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Thanks to technology, many things that once took hours now take minutes.","note":"Thanks to 引出正面影响；took hours → take minutes 对比鲜明。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We can pay bills, book tickets and attend classes without leaving home, and information that used to hide in libraries is now at our fingertips.","note":"三个动词并列举例；at our fingertips（触手可及）是科技题高频好词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Admittedly, technology also creates complications.","note":"Admittedly 让步短句，开启反面，节奏好。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Endless messages demand our attention, passwords and updates never seem to stop, and older people often struggle to keep up with new devices.","note":"三个具体细节并列，「复杂」写得看得见；keep up with（跟上）准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, most of these problems come from how we use technology, not from technology itself.","note":"全文的立意句：问题在用法不在科技本身，辩证落点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"With reasonable habits, such as turning off unnecessary notices, the troubles can be reduced greatly.","note":"such as 给出具体习惯，建议落地。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, technology is a tool that serves life.","note":"结尾先给总定位，短句有力。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It makes life simpler for those who learn to control it.","note":"those who… 定语从句收尾，把结论限定在「会控制它的人」，呼应立意句。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Modern technology surrounds us in almost every part of life, yet people hold different views on whether it has made life simpler or more complicated. Personally, I believe technology has made life simpler in most ways, though it does bring new troubles.","Thanks to technology, many things that once took hours now take minutes. We can pay bills, book tickets and attend classes without leaving home, and information that used to hide in libraries is now at our fingertips. Admittedly, technology also creates complications. Endless messages demand our attention, passwords and updates never seem to stop, and older people often struggle to keep up with new devices. However, most of these problems come from how we use technology, not from technology itself. With reasonable habits, such as turning off unnecessary notices, the troubles can be reduced greatly.","In conclusion, technology is a tool that serves life. It makes life simpler for those who learn to control it."],"id":"tech-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people think modern technology has made life simpler, while others believe it has made life more complicated. What is your opinion? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"科技让生活更简单还是更复杂","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In recent years, live-stream shopping has swept across China.","note":"swept across（席卷）一个动词把「走红」写活，现象类开头出彩靠动词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Millions of people watch hosts introduce products on their phones and place orders within seconds, turning shopping into a form of entertainment.","note":"描述现象的具体画面 + turning…into… 分词短语点出本质变化。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Several reasons explain its popularity.","note":"原因段总起句，简洁。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, live-stream shopping is interactive.","note":"interactive（互动的）是这个话题的关键词，一词点中第一条原因。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Unlike traditional online shops, it allows buyers to ask questions and watch products being used in real time, which builds trust.","note":"Unlike… 对比开头；in real time（实时地）；which 从句点出结果「建立信任」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, attractive prices and limited-time discounts create a strong sense of urgency, encouraging people to buy quickly.","note":"a sense of urgency（紧迫感）是准搭配；encouraging 分词补结果。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Moreover, watching a friendly host chat and perform makes shopping relaxing and fun, especially for young people under pressure.","note":"动名词作主语；第三条原因落到「解压」，角度比价格更深一层。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, live-stream shopping is a creative business model, but buyers should stay rational.","note":"评论段先肯定再提醒，stay rational（保持理性）是消费话题的落点词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Before clicking the buy button, we should ask ourselves whether we truly need the product, instead of buying on impulse.","note":"on impulse（冲动地）收尾，建议具体到「点按钮之前先问自己」。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["In recent years, live-stream shopping has swept across China. Millions of people watch hosts introduce products on their phones and place orders within seconds, turning shopping into a form of entertainment.","Several reasons explain its popularity. First, live-stream shopping is interactive. Unlike traditional online shops, it allows buyers to ask questions and watch products being used in real time, which builds trust. Second, attractive prices and limited-time discounts create a strong sense of urgency, encouraging people to buy quickly. Moreover, watching a friendly host chat and perform makes shopping relaxing and fun, especially for young people under pressure.","In my view, live-stream shopping is a creative business model, but buyers should stay rational. Before clicking the buy button, we should ask ourselves whether we truly need the product, instead of buying on impulse."],"id":"tech-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Live-stream shopping has become extremely popular in recent years. Analyze the reasons for its popularity and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"直播购物走红","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Nowadays, more and more college students spend too much time on their mobile phones.","note":"第一句直接提出问题，问题解决型的开头不绕弯。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This problem has caused a lot of worries.","note":"短句点明问题值得重视，自然过渡到分析段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, many students use their phones in class.","note":"First / Second 分层，危害一条一条说清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They play games or chat with friends instead of listening to the teacher, so they cannot follow the lessons.","note":"instead of listening 对比出课堂上的具体危害；follow the lessons（跟上课）搭配准确。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, some students stay up late playing with their phones, and they feel tired the next day.","note":"stay up late（熬夜）是这个话题的必备词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"As a result, their studies and health are both harmed.","note":"As a result 收束危害：学业和健康两头都点到。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To solve this problem, students should first learn to control themselves.","note":"To solve this problem 是问题解决型对策段的标志句，看到题目就该想到它。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For example, they can put their phones away during class and set a time limit for entertainment.","note":"建议带具体做法：put away（收起来）、set a time limit（设定时限），不空喊「要自律」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, colleges can organize more sports and social activities, so students will have less free time for their phones.","note":"第二条建议换主体（学校），对策不只靠个人，角度更全。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In conclusion, mobile phones are useful tools, but we should use them wisely.","note":"结尾辩证定位：工具本身没错，关键在用法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Only in this way can we make the best of them.","note":"Only in this way can we… 倒装收尾，make the best of（充分利用）点题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Nowadays, more and more college students spend too much time on their mobile phones. This problem has caused a lot of worries.","First, many students use their phones in class. They play games or chat with friends instead of listening to the teacher, so they cannot follow the lessons. Second, some students stay up late playing with their phones, and they feel tired the next day. As a result, their studies and health are both harmed.","To solve this problem, students should first learn to control themselves. For example, they can put their phones away during class and set a time limit for entertainment. Besides, colleges can organize more sports and social activities, so students will have less free time for their phones.","In conclusion, mobile phones are useful tools, but we should use them wisely. Only in this way can we make the best of them."],"id":"tech-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Nowadays, more and more college students spend too much time on their mobile phones. Please write a composition of 120–180 words to discuss the problem and suggest some solutions.（问题解决型：提出问题 + 分析原因 + 提出建议）","source":"模拟题（原备好的写作第 4 题草稿）","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"大学生沉迷手机","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Learning English well requires daily practice, and a good app can make this much easier.","note":"介绍类短文先讲需求再引出产品，读者立刻知道这篇写什么。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The app I want to introduce is called English Daily, which has been my English partner for almost a year.","note":"is called… 报出名字；which 从句补一句自己的使用经历，可信度上来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This app has three features that I find most useful.","note":"预告三点，主体段骨架先立住——介绍文最稳的写法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, it pushes a short news report every morning, read slowly and clearly, which is perfect for listening practice on the bus.","note":"push（推送）是 App 话题的准动词；细节落到「在公交车上练听力」，画面感强。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, it builds a personal word list from the words I look up, and reminds me to review them before I forget.","note":"look up（查词）、remind sb to do，把功能写成使用场景而不是说明书。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Third, it records my study time and shows my progress week by week, which keeps me motivated.","note":"week by week（逐周）地道；keep me motivated 点出功能带来的好处。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The basic functions are free, and the design is simple and clean.","note":"补一句价格和设计，介绍更完整，短句收束主体段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If you are looking for a helper in English learning, why not give English Daily a try?","note":"Why not…? 反问句向读者发出邀请，介绍文的经典收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Small efforts every day will add up to real progress.","note":"add up to（累积成）收尾升华，一句格言味的话结束全文。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Learning English well requires daily practice, and a good app can make this much easier. The app I want to introduce is called English Daily, which has been my English partner for almost a year.","This app has three features that I find most useful. First, it pushes a short news report every morning, read slowly and clearly, which is perfect for listening practice on the bus. Second, it builds a personal word list from the words I look up, and reminds me to review them before I forget. Third, it records my study time and shows my progress week by week, which keeps me motivated. The basic functions are free, and the design is simple and clean.","If you are looking for a helper in English learning, why not give English Daily a try? Small efforts every day will add up to real progress."],"id":"tech-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Your university newspaper is collecting articles introducing useful apps for study. Write an article of 120–180 words to introduce an English-learning app that you often use.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"短文：介绍一款学习 App","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Whether students should be allowed to use AI tools for homework has become a heated topic.","note":"Whether… 主语从句开头，把题目本身变成话题，观点类高级起手。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, AI tools can be used for homework, but only as a helper in the learning process, never as a replacement for students' own work.","note":"表态带限定：helper 而非 replacement，立场有边界、不走极端。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used properly, AI can support learning in real ways.","note":"分词短语开头开启正面段，主题句简洁。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When a student is stuck on a difficult problem late at night, AI can offer hints step by step, much like a patient tutor.","note":"具体场景（深夜被难题卡住）+ 比喻（耐心的家教），好处写得可感。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It can also check grammar and suggest better expressions, from which students learn actively.","note":"from which 定语从句，正式且紧凑。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, copying AI-generated answers directly is a completely different matter.","note":"转折句划清界限：使用 ≠ 抄袭，这是全文的立意关键。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Homework exists to train the mind; if a machine does all the thinking, students learn nothing and even develop the bad habit of dishonesty.","note":"分号 + 条件句讲清危害的逻辑链，最后落到 dishonesty（不诚实）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Schools should therefore set clear rules: AI may guide and check, but the final work must come from the student himself.","note":"冒号引出规则内容，对策具体，文章不止于表态。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In short, the question is not whether to use AI, but how to use it honestly and wisely.","note":"not whether…but how… 对比收尾，把争议提升一层。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Whether students should be allowed to use AI tools for homework has become a heated topic. In my opinion, AI tools can be used for homework, but only as a helper in the learning process, never as a replacement for students' own work.","Used properly, AI can support learning in real ways. When a student is stuck on a difficult problem late at night, AI can offer hints step by step, much like a patient tutor. It can also check grammar and suggest better expressions, from which students learn actively. However, copying AI-generated answers directly is a completely different matter. Homework exists to train the mind; if a machine does all the thinking, students learn nothing and even develop the bad habit of dishonesty. Schools should therefore set clear rules: AI may guide and check, but the final work must come from the student himself.","In short, the question is not whether to use AI, but how to use it honestly and wisely."],"id":"tech-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some students use AI tools to finish their homework, which has caused wide concern. Should students be allowed to use AI tools for homework? State your view in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"该不该用 AI 工具写作业","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Social media has changed the way young people make friends.","note":"一句话点出变化，利弊类开头直奔主题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Instead of meeting only in classrooms or neighborhoods, they now connect with people from all over the world with a simple click.","note":"instead of 对比过去与现在；with a simple click 画面感强。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Making friends online has clear advantages.","note":"动名词作主语，主题句开启正面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It breaks the limits of distance and helps shy people express themselves more freely.","note":"break the limits of（打破……的限制）是好搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Through shared interests, such as music or games, strangers can quickly become close friends.","note":"shared interests（共同兴趣）是社交话题准词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, the disadvantages should not be overlooked.","note":"转折短句开启负面段，be overlooked（被忽视）正式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"People online may not be who they appear to be, and personal information can be misused by strangers with bad intentions.","note":"appear to be（表面上是）+ be misused by 被动句，风险写得准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, spending too much time on virtual friendship may weaken real-life relationships, leaving some young people lonely in the real world.","note":"virtual（虚拟的）与 real-life 对照；leaving… 分词补结果。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, online friendship is a useful extension of social life, but it cannot replace face-to-face communication.","note":"extension（延伸）定位精准：是补充不是替代，利弊类结论的典范。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We should enjoy its convenience while staying careful and keeping a balance.","note":"while + 两个动名词并列收尾，建议全面。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Social media has changed the way young people make friends. Instead of meeting only in classrooms or neighborhoods, they now connect with people from all over the world with a simple click.","Making friends online has clear advantages. It breaks the limits of distance and helps shy people express themselves more freely. Through shared interests, such as music or games, strangers can quickly become close friends. However, the disadvantages should not be overlooked. People online may not be who they appear to be, and personal information can be misused by strangers with bad intentions. Besides, spending too much time on virtual friendship may weaken real-life relationships, leaving some young people lonely in the real world.","In conclusion, online friendship is a useful extension of social life, but it cannot replace face-to-face communication. We should enjoy its convenience while staying careful and keeping a balance."],"id":"tech-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many young people make friends on social media. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of making friends online and give your conclusion in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"在社交媒体上交朋友","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"A few years ago, a wallet was a must when going out.","note":"从过去的一个小细节切入，a must（必备品）说法地道。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Today, however, many Chinese people travel, shop and eat all day with nothing but a mobile phone, as cashless payment has become part of daily life.","note":"三个动词并列 + nothing but（只有）对比今昔，现象一句说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This change has taken place for good reasons.","note":"take place（发生）开启原因段，过渡自然。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Mobile payment is fast and convenient: a quick scan finishes a deal in seconds, and neither side needs to worry about change or fake money.","note":"冒号展开解释；change 在这里是「零钱」，一词多义用对了显功底。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It is also safer, since carrying large amounts of cash is no longer necessary.","note":"since 引导原因；no longer（不再）正式替换 not…anymore。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"As a result, our life has become more efficient in many ways.","note":"As a result 切换到「影响」部分，现象类后半程的标志词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Small shops save the cost of handling cash, and every payment record helps people manage their money better.","note":"两个具体好处并列，影响写得落地。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Nevertheless, problems exist.","note":"Nevertheless 转折短句，开启问题面，文章不一边倒。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Older people who are not familiar with smartphones may find themselves in difficulty, and a dead battery or poor signal can leave a person unable to pay.","note":"be familiar with、find oneself in difficulty，两个具体困境把问题写实。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, cashless payment is a welcome progress, but society should also keep cash available for those who need it.","note":"结论带人文关怀：进步要欢迎，也要给跟不上的人留路——立意加分。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["A few years ago, a wallet was a must when going out. Today, however, many Chinese people travel, shop and eat all day with nothing but a mobile phone, as cashless payment has become part of daily life.","This change has taken place for good reasons. Mobile payment is fast and convenient: a quick scan finishes a deal in seconds, and neither side needs to worry about change or fake money. It is also safer, since carrying large amounts of cash is no longer necessary. As a result, our life has become more efficient in many ways. Small shops save the cost of handling cash, and every payment record helps people manage their money better. Nevertheless, problems exist. Older people who are not familiar with smartphones may find themselves in difficulty, and a dead battery or poor signal can leave a person unable to pay.","In short, cashless payment is a welcome progress, but society should also keep cash available for those who need it."],"id":"tech-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: In China today, people can go out all day without any cash, paying for everything with their phones. Analyze the reasons for this phenomenon and its effects in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"无现金社会","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In the Internet age, personal information leaks have become a serious problem.","note":"一句点明问题，问题解决型标准开头。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Phone numbers, addresses and even bank details are collected by various apps, and once leaked, they may cause endless trouble.","note":"被动语态 are collected 符合「信息被收集」的事实；once leaked 分词短语紧凑。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The risks are obvious.","note":"短句总起危害段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With leaked information, criminals can send cheating messages that look real, steal money from accounts, or disturb people's daily life with endless sales calls.","note":"三个动词并列列举危害，从诈骗到骚扰，层层具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What is worse, many users have weak awareness of protection: they use the same simple password everywhere and connect to unknown Wi-Fi without a second thought.","note":"What is worse 递进；without a second thought（想都不想）把「意识弱」写活。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To protect ourselves, we should first give out as little personal information as possible and read permission requests carefully before agreeing.","note":"对策段 To protect ourselves 开头；as little…as possible 是准句式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Besides, different and stronger passwords should be set for important accounts, and suspicious links should never be clicked.","note":"被动语态连用，suspicious（可疑的）是安全话题准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In a word, in an age when information is valuable, protecting it carefully is protecting ourselves.","note":"when 定语从句 + 对仗收尾（保护信息就是保护自己），立意拔高。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In the Internet age, personal information leaks have become a serious problem. Phone numbers, addresses and even bank details are collected by various apps, and once leaked, they may cause endless trouble.","The risks are obvious. With leaked information, criminals can send cheating messages that look real, steal money from accounts, or disturb people's daily life with endless sales calls. What is worse, many users have weak awareness of protection: they use the same simple password everywhere and connect to unknown Wi-Fi without a second thought.","To protect ourselves, we should first give out as little personal information as possible and read permission requests carefully before agreeing. Besides, different and stronger passwords should be set for important accounts, and suspicious links should never be clicked. In a word, in an age when information is valuable, protecting it carefully is protecting ourselves."],"id":"tech-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Personal information leaks happen frequently in the Internet age. What are the risks, and how can we protect our personal information? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"technology","themeName":"科技","title":"个人信息泄露","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Plastic bags, bottles and boxes are everywhere in our daily life.","note":"三个具体名词开头，现象不用抽象讲，画面先出来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"While they bring us convenience, the pollution they cause has become a serious problem that can no longer be ignored.","note":"While 让步句一转，从方便转到污染；can no longer be ignored 是环境题标志说法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The harms of plastic pollution are clear.","note":"短句总起危害段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Plastic waste is extremely hard to break down; a single plastic bag may stay in the soil for hundreds of years, damaging the land and water around it.","note":"break down（分解）是塑料话题的核心词；hundreds of years 用时间尺度讲危害。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Animals in rivers and oceans often mistake plastic for food, and many die as a result.","note":"mistake A for B（把 A 误认为 B）准搭配；as a result 收束因果。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"What is worse, tiny plastic particles may finally enter our own food and drinking water, threatening human health in ways we are only beginning to understand.","note":"What is worse 递进到人类自身；particles（微粒）用词准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To reduce plastic pollution, action is needed from everyone.","note":"对策段开头点明「人人有责」，为三方分工做铺垫。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The government should limit the use of single-use plastic products, shops should offer greener choices, and we ourselves should carry cloth bags and refuse unnecessary packaging.","note":"政府、商家、个人三方并列，对策全面；single-use（一次性的）是准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Small changes, repeated by millions of people, will make a big difference.","note":"make a big difference 收尾，环境题最实用的结尾句之一。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Plastic bags, bottles and boxes are everywhere in our daily life. While they bring us convenience, the pollution they cause has become a serious problem that can no longer be ignored.","The harms of plastic pollution are clear. Plastic waste is extremely hard to break down; a single plastic bag may stay in the soil for hundreds of years, damaging the land and water around it. Animals in rivers and oceans often mistake plastic for food, and many die as a result. What is worse, tiny plastic particles may finally enter our own food and drinking water, threatening human health in ways we are only beginning to understand.","To reduce plastic pollution, action is needed from everyone. The government should limit the use of single-use plastic products, shops should offer greener choices, and we ourselves should carry cloth bags and refuse unnecessary packaging. Small changes, repeated by millions of people, will make a big difference."],"id":"env-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Plastic products are widely used in daily life, but plastic pollution has become a serious problem. Analyze the harms of plastic pollution and give your suggestions in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"塑料污染","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Water covers most of the earth, yet fresh water that people can actually use is limited, and many regions are already facing serious shortages.","note":"yet 转折制造反差：水多但可用水少，问题一句立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some people believe saving water is only the government's business.","note":"摆出对方观点，为反驳做靶子。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I cannot agree with this view.","note":"短句表态干脆，观点类第一段就要这样明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is true that the government should do its part: building reservoirs, repairing leaking pipes and setting proper water prices.","note":"It is true that… 先让步承认政府的作用；冒号后三个动名词列具体职责。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"But the largest amount of water is used and wasted in daily life by millions of ordinary people.","note":"But 转折回主线：最大的使用和浪费在日常生活。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A tap left running while brushing teeth, a long shower, a half-full washing machine — each waste looks tiny, but multiplied by billions of people, it becomes an ocean.","note":"三个生活细节排比 + multiplied by（乘以亿万人）算出总量，it becomes an ocean 收得漂亮。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Saving water, therefore, starts with small habits: turning off taps tightly, reusing water where possible and choosing water-saving devices at home.","note":"therefore 承接推论；三个动名词给出可执行的小习惯。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, the government builds the system, but every drop is saved or wasted in our own hands.","note":"every drop（每一滴）双关收尾，政府与个人各归其位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Protecting water resources is truly everyone's responsibility.","note":"动名词作主语重申主题句，与标题呼应。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Water covers most of the earth, yet fresh water that people can actually use is limited, and many regions are already facing serious shortages. Some people believe saving water is only the government's business. I cannot agree with this view.","It is true that the government should do its part: building reservoirs, repairing leaking pipes and setting proper water prices. But the largest amount of water is used and wasted in daily life by millions of ordinary people. A tap left running while brushing teeth, a long shower, a half-full washing machine — each waste looks tiny, but multiplied by billions of people, it becomes an ocean. Saving water, therefore, starts with small habits: turning off taps tightly, reusing water where possible and choosing water-saving devices at home.","In conclusion, the government builds the system, but every drop is saved or wasted in our own hands. Protecting water resources is truly everyone's responsibility."],"id":"env-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Water shortages are becoming serious in many parts of the world. Some people think saving water is only the government's concern. Do you agree? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"节约用水，人人有责","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Garbage sorting has become a hot topic since many cities made it a rule, with fines for those who refuse to follow it.","note":"with fines（带罚款）一句交代政策背景；garbage sorting 是本主题必备词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Although sorting garbage takes extra time and effort, I strongly support this policy.","note":"Although 先让步再表态，第一段立场鲜明。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, sorting is the first step toward recycling.","note":"理由一主题句：分类是回收的第一步，逻辑起点清楚。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When waste is separated properly, useful materials such as paper, metal and glass can be reused instead of being buried or burned, which saves resources and reduces pollution.","note":"被动语态连用符合客观叙述；which 从句点出最终好处，一句顶三句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Moreover, a clear rule with fines helps people form the habit quickly.","note":"form the habit（养成习惯）准搭配；理由二落到「习惯」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Experience from many cities shows that most residents get used to sorting within months, and what begins as a duty soon becomes a natural part of life.","note":"用其他城市的经验作论据；what 主语从句把「义务变自然」讲得漂亮。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A cleaner environment also means lower costs for the whole society in the long run.","note":"in the long run（长远来看）补上经济角度，理由更全。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, garbage sorting may be a little troublesome at first, but its benefits far outweigh the trouble.","note":"far outweigh（远远超过）收尾表态，呼应首段的让步。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A small effort from each family leads to a cleaner city for everyone.","note":"lead to 收尾升华：每家的小努力 → 全城的大改变。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Garbage sorting has become a hot topic since many cities made it a rule, with fines for those who refuse to follow it. Although sorting garbage takes extra time and effort, I strongly support this policy.","To begin with, sorting is the first step toward recycling. When waste is separated properly, useful materials such as paper, metal and glass can be reused instead of being buried or burned, which saves resources and reduces pollution. Moreover, a clear rule with fines helps people form the habit quickly. Experience from many cities shows that most residents get used to sorting within months, and what begins as a duty soon becomes a natural part of life. A cleaner environment also means lower costs for the whole society in the long run.","In conclusion, garbage sorting may be a little troublesome at first, but its benefits far outweigh the trouble. A small effort from each family leads to a cleaner city for everyone."],"id":"env-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many cities now require residents to sort their garbage, and those who fail to do so may be fined. Do you support this policy? Write 120–180 words to state your view.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"垃圾分类该不该强制","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Private cars, once a luxury, have entered millions of ordinary families in China.","note":"once a luxury（曾经的奢侈品）插入语，一句写出变化之大。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Their rapid growth has brought both convenience and serious problems to city life.","note":"预告利弊两面，利弊类标准第二句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, owning a car makes travel far more comfortable and flexible.","note":"动名词作主语 + On the one hand，骨架词到位。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Families can go out whenever they like, carry heavy things easily and travel to places that buses cannot reach.","note":"三个动词并列，好具体；that 定语从句补细节。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The car industry also creates a large number of jobs.","note":"补一条经济角度的好处，分析更全面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the other hand, too many cars are choking our cities.","note":"choke（堵死、窒息）一个动词把拥堵写活。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Traffic jams waste people's time every morning, finding a parking space has become a daily headache, and exhaust gas from cars is a major source of air pollution.","note":"三个坏处并列：堵车、停车、尾气；exhaust gas（尾气）是环境话题准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In big cities especially, the cost of more cars is becoming higher than the convenience they bring.","note":"cost 与 convenience 对比，为结论段的判断埋伏笔。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, private cars should be used in a smarter way.","note":"结论不搞一刀切禁用，而是「更聪明地用」，有分寸。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Developing public transport and encouraging green travel will help cities enjoy the benefits of cars without suffering too much from them.","note":"两个动名词并列给出对策；green travel（绿色出行）收尾扣题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Private cars, once a luxury, have entered millions of ordinary families in China. Their rapid growth has brought both convenience and serious problems to city life.","On the one hand, owning a car makes travel far more comfortable and flexible. Families can go out whenever they like, carry heavy things easily and travel to places that buses cannot reach. The car industry also creates a large number of jobs. On the other hand, too many cars are choking our cities. Traffic jams waste people's time every morning, finding a parking space has become a daily headache, and exhaust gas from cars is a major source of air pollution. In big cities especially, the cost of more cars is becoming higher than the convenience they bring.","In my view, private cars should be used in a smarter way. Developing public transport and encouraging green travel will help cities enjoy the benefits of cars without suffering too much from them."],"id":"env-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: The number of private cars keeps growing in Chinese cities. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this trend and give your conclusion in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"私家车越来越多","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Walk around any campus and you will see waste in many forms: lights burning in empty classrooms, plates of food thrown away untouched, and taps left running.","note":"祈使句开头带读者进场景；冒号后三个具体画面，问题不用抽象讲。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Such waste is a serious problem that we should not take for granted.","note":"take for granted（习以为常、理所当然）是高频好词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To solve it, efforts are needed on several sides.","note":"对策段总起：多方努力，预告下文分工。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, the university should build a saving culture.","note":"第一条对策先给定位（文化），再给做法，层次清楚。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Posters, lectures and activities during Earth Week can remind students that resources are limited and precious.","note":"三个名词并列举例；remind sb that… 句型实用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, practical rules can help.","note":"短句主题句，第二条对策换角度：靠制度。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For example, canteens can offer smaller portions so that students take only what they can eat, and dormitories can reward rooms that use less electricity.","note":"两个具体做法并列：小份菜、用电奖励——建议可执行才有分。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Most importantly, every student should develop the habit of saving in daily life: turning off lights when leaving, finishing the food on the plate and using both sides of paper.","note":"Most importantly 把最重要一条放最后；三个动名词与开头画面一一呼应。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In a word, waste on campus is not a small matter.","note":"In a word 收尾重申，短句定调。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When saving becomes a habit for everyone, our campus will be a greener and better place.","note":"when 从句展望结尾，把「习惯」与「绿色校园」扣回主题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Walk around any campus and you will see waste in many forms: lights burning in empty classrooms, plates of food thrown away untouched, and taps left running. Such waste is a serious problem that we should not take for granted.","To solve it, efforts are needed on several sides. First, the university should build a saving culture. Posters, lectures and activities during Earth Week can remind students that resources are limited and precious. Second, practical rules can help. For example, canteens can offer smaller portions so that students take only what they can eat, and dormitories can reward rooms that use less electricity. Most importantly, every student should develop the habit of saving in daily life: turning off lights when leaving, finishing the food on the plate and using both sides of paper.","In a word, waste on campus is not a small matter. When saving becomes a habit for everyone, our campus will be a greener and better place."],"id":"env-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Waste can be seen everywhere on campus: lights left on in empty classrooms, food thrown away in canteens, and water running for nothing. How can this problem be solved? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"校园里的浪费现象","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear fellow students,","note":"倡议书称呼：fellow students（同学们），对象明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Our campus is our second home, but its environment needs our care.","note":"second home 比喻拉近距离，倡议书先动情再讲理。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Bottles are left on lawns, lights stay on in empty classrooms, and too much food is wasted every day.","note":"三个具体问题并列（被动+主动混用），倡议的理由看得见。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To build a green campus, the Students' Union proposes the following to all students.","note":"propose the following 是倡议书的标志句，引出分点内容。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, let us reduce waste in daily life.","note":"倡议分点用 let us（让我们）开头，语气是号召不是命令。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Carry your own bottle and bag, choose smaller portions in the canteen, and turn off lights and taps when they are not needed.","note":"三个祈使动作并列，倡议落到人人能做的小事上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, let us keep our campus clean and green.","note":"第二条换角度：从节约到爱护，分点不重复。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Do not litter, take part in tree-planting and cleaning activities, and remind others kindly when they harm the environment.","note":"litter（乱扔垃圾）准词；remind others kindly 加了 kindly，倡议有温度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, let us travel green: walk or ride bicycles for short distances instead of taking cars.","note":"travel green 短语新颖；冒号后解释清楚。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A green campus begins with each of us.","note":"收尾号召句，短而有力，倡议书的点睛之笔。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Let us take action from now on and make our campus cleaner, greener and more beautiful.","note":"take action（采取行动）+ 三个比较级并列，最后落款 The Students' Union——格式完整。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear fellow students,","Our campus is our second home, but its environment needs our care. Bottles are left on lawns, lights stay on in empty classrooms, and too much food is wasted every day. To build a green campus, the Students' Union proposes the following to all students.","First, let us reduce waste in daily life. Carry your own bottle and bag, choose smaller portions in the canteen, and turn off lights and taps when they are not needed. Second, let us keep our campus clean and green. Do not litter, take part in tree-planting and cleaning activities, and remind others kindly when they harm the environment. Third, let us travel green: walk or ride bicycles for short distances instead of taking cars.","A green campus begins with each of us. Let us take action from now on and make our campus cleaner, greener and more beautiful.","The Students' Union"],"id":"env-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: The Students' Union of your university is calling for a green campus. Write a proposal (倡议书) of 120–180 words to call on students to protect the campus environment. Sign it as the Students' Union.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"倡议书：绿色校园","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"When it comes to protecting the environment, a question is often raised: is it the government's duty or everyone's duty?","note":"When it comes to… + 冒号引出争议问题，观点类开头有悬念。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, the government plays the leading role, but real change is impossible without the participation of every individual.","note":"表态是「两边都要、以政府为主」，participation（参与）用词正式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The government has powers that individuals do not have.","note":"主题句先行，先讲政府不可替代之处。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It can make laws to punish factories that pollute rivers, invest in public transport and support clean energy with huge funds.","note":"三个动词并列：立法、投资、扶持；clean energy（清洁能源）准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Without such actions, environmental problems cannot be solved at a national level.","note":"Without 虚拟条件强调不可或缺；at a national level 拔高视角。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, the government alone is not enough.","note":"短句转折开启个人部分，alone 一个词点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Pollution comes largely from daily life: the cars we drive, the plastic we throw away and the electricity we waste.","note":"冒号 + 三个「我们」的生活细节，论证落到地面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If billions of daily choices go in the wrong direction, no policy can fully succeed.","note":"if 条件句讲清个人与政策的关系，逻辑严密。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"When each person saves a little water and uses a little less plastic, the combined effect is enormous.","note":"combined effect（叠加效应）是这个论点的点睛词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, protecting the environment requires both strong policies from above and small actions from everyone.","note":"both…and… 收束两方，from above / from everyone 对照工整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Only together can they keep our planet green.","note":"Only together can they… 倒装短句收尾，干脆有力。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["When it comes to protecting the environment, a question is often raised: is it the government's duty or everyone's duty? In my view, the government plays the leading role, but real change is impossible without the participation of every individual.","The government has powers that individuals do not have. It can make laws to punish factories that pollute rivers, invest in public transport and support clean energy with huge funds. Without such actions, environmental problems cannot be solved at a national level. However, the government alone is not enough. Pollution comes largely from daily life: the cars we drive, the plastic we throw away and the electricity we waste. If billions of daily choices go in the wrong direction, no policy can fully succeed. When each person saves a little water and uses a little less plastic, the combined effect is enormous.","In conclusion, protecting the environment requires both strong policies from above and small actions from everyone. Only together can they keep our planet green."],"id":"env-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people believe environmental protection is mainly the government's job, while others argue that every individual should take responsibility. What is your opinion? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"保护环境靠政府还是靠个人","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In the past few years, new energy vehicles have appeared on Chinese roads in rapidly growing numbers.","note":"In the past few years + 现在完成时，现象类稳妥开头。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Green license plates, once a rare sight, can now be seen in almost every city.","note":"用一个看得见的细节（绿牌）印证现象，比数据更生动。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Their popularity is easy to explain.","note":"短句开启原因段，过渡干净。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, new energy vehicles are much cheaper to run, since electricity costs far less than petrol for the same distance.","note":"since 引导原因；for the same distance 对比口径一致，论证严谨。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In addition, the government offers strong support, including purchase subsidies and easier license plates in big cities.","note":"subsidies（补贴）是政策类准词；including 列举具体支持。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Most importantly, growing environmental awareness makes many buyers willing to choose a cleaner way to travel.","note":"Most importantly 把最深层原因放最后：环保意识——原因分析有层次。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The effects on the environment are positive in general.","note":"切换到「影响」部分的总起句，in general 留有分寸。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Electric cars produce no exhaust gas on the road, which helps improve city air.","note":"exhaust gas（尾气）；which 从句点出好处。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, we should also notice that producing batteries costs energy and used batteries need careful treatment.","note":"补上电池的另一面，分析不一边倒，显得客观。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On the whole, new energy vehicles are a step in the right direction, and with cleaner power and better recycling, they will become greener still.","note":"a step in the right direction（朝正确方向迈出的一步）收尾定性，with 短语展望。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In the past few years, new energy vehicles have appeared on Chinese roads in rapidly growing numbers. Green license plates, once a rare sight, can now be seen in almost every city.","Their popularity is easy to explain. To begin with, new energy vehicles are much cheaper to run, since electricity costs far less than petrol for the same distance. In addition, the government offers strong support, including purchase subsidies and easier license plates in big cities. Most importantly, growing environmental awareness makes many buyers willing to choose a cleaner way to travel. The effects on the environment are positive in general. Electric cars produce no exhaust gas on the road, which helps improve city air. However, we should also notice that producing batteries costs energy and used batteries need careful treatment.","On the whole, new energy vehicles are a step in the right direction, and with cleaner power and better recycling, they will become greener still."],"id":"env-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: New energy vehicles are becoming increasingly common on Chinese roads. Analyze the reasons for their popularity and their effects on the environment in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"新能源汽车走红","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Disposable products are part of modern life.","note":"短句开篇，disposable（一次性的）是本篇关键词，先点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We use a plastic cup once and throw it away, eat with wooden chopsticks once and drop them in the bin, enjoying convenience without thinking much about the cost.","note":"两个生活动作并列 + enjoying 分词，把「便利」写成画面；cost 一语双关，引出下文。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The advantages are obvious.","note":"短句开启正面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Disposable products are cheap, clean and convenient; they save time and effort, and in hospitals and restaurants they help prevent the spread of disease.","note":"三个形容词并列 + 分号展开；prevent the spread of disease 是加分的具体好处，不空泛。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For busy people in fast-moving cities, they seem almost necessary.","note":"almost necessary 把正面推到顶点，为转折蓄势。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, their disadvantages are far more serious.","note":"转折句直接定调：坏处更严重——利弊类要有倾向，不要两边一样重。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Most disposable products are used for only a few minutes but take hundreds of years to break down.","note":"a few minutes ↔ hundreds of years，时间对比是全篇最有力的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The production of disposable chopsticks alone consumes huge numbers of trees every year.","note":"alone（仅仅）强调；consume（消耗）比 use 高级。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Mountains of plastic waste are filling our land and flowing into our rivers and oceans.","note":"mountains of（堆积如山的）形象化，危害收束有画面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, convenience should not come at the cost of the environment.","note":"at the cost of（以……为代价）是环境题的核心句式，值得背。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Disposable products should be limited to situations where they are truly needed, and reusable choices should become our first choice in daily life.","note":"结论给两条具体主张：限制使用 + 可重复使用优先，不搞全盘否定。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Disposable products are part of modern life. We use a plastic cup once and throw it away, eat with wooden chopsticks once and drop them in the bin, enjoying convenience without thinking much about the cost.","The advantages are obvious. Disposable products are cheap, clean and convenient; they save time and effort, and in hospitals and restaurants they help prevent the spread of disease. For busy people in fast-moving cities, they seem almost necessary. However, their disadvantages are far more serious. Most disposable products are used for only a few minutes but take hundreds of years to break down. The production of disposable chopsticks alone consumes huge numbers of trees every year. Mountains of plastic waste are filling our land and flowing into our rivers and oceans.","In my view, convenience should not come at the cost of the environment. Disposable products should be limited to situations where they are truly needed, and reusable choices should become our first choice in daily life."],"id":"env-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Disposable products, such as plastic cups, chopsticks and bags, are widely used in daily life. Discuss their advantages and disadvantages in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"一次性用品的便利与危害","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Although the air in many cities has improved in recent years, air pollution is still a serious problem.","note":"Although 先肯定改善再点问题，开头客观、不夸大。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On bad days, a grey sky hangs over the city and people put on masks before going out.","note":"一个画面句把问题写实：灰天 + 口罩。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Several causes lie behind the problem.","note":"lie behind（是……背后的原因）总起原因段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Vehicle exhaust is a major source, as the number of cars keeps rising.","note":"exhaust（尾气）准词；as 引导原因，简洁。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Factories and construction sites produce dust and harmful gases, and in northern cities, burning coal for heating in winter makes the air even worse.","note":"两个来源并列，再补北方供暖的特殊原因，分析全面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To improve air quality, measures must be taken from different sides.","note":"measures must be taken 被动句开启对策段，环境题标志句式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The government should set stricter standards for factories and vehicles and develop clean energy step by step.","note":"set standards（制定标准）；step by step 显得务实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Cities should build better public transport so that fewer people need to drive.","note":"so that 目的从句，对策与原因（汽车尾气）前后呼应。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"As individuals, we can choose buses, subways or bicycles for short trips and report serious pollution when we see it.","note":"对策落到个人层面，三方分工完整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Clean air will not return in a day, but with continuous effort from society as a whole, blue skies will become a normal part of city life again.","note":"not…in a day 化用「非一日之功」；blue skies 意象收尾，有余味。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Although the air in many cities has improved in recent years, air pollution is still a serious problem. On bad days, a grey sky hangs over the city and people put on masks before going out.","Several causes lie behind the problem. Vehicle exhaust is a major source, as the number of cars keeps rising. Factories and construction sites produce dust and harmful gases, and in northern cities, burning coal for heating in winter makes the air even worse. To improve air quality, measures must be taken from different sides. The government should set stricter standards for factories and vehicles and develop clean energy step by step. Cities should build better public transport so that fewer people need to drive. As individuals, we can choose buses, subways or bicycles for short trips and report serious pollution when we see it.","Clean air will not return in a day, but with continuous effort from society as a whole, blue skies will become a normal part of city life again."],"id":"env-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Air pollution remains a serious problem in many cities. What causes it, and what measures can be taken to improve air quality? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"environment","themeName":"环境","title":"城市空气污染","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"On any night in a university dormitory, the lights of phone screens can be seen long after midnight.","note":"场景开头：宿舍里午夜的手机光，现象不用解释就立住了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Staying up late has become a shared habit among college students, and it is quietly harming their health and study.","note":"stay up late 是健康主题的头号词组；quietly harming（悄悄损害）写出危害的隐蔽性。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"There are several reasons behind this habit.","note":"原因段总起句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Heavy study tasks and part-time jobs take up the daytime, so students push their entertainment and social life into the night.","note":"take up（占用）+ push…into the night，原因写得合情合理，不是简单怪手机。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Phones make the problem worse: one more video or one more game easily steals an hour without being noticed.","note":"one more… 排比细节；steals an hour（偷走一小时）拟人，生动。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The effects are serious.","note":"短句切换到影响部分，现象类后半程标志。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students who sleep too little feel sleepy in class, remember less of what they learn, and become weak and anxious over time.","note":"三个后果并列：课堂、记忆、身心；over time（久而久之）收尾。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Some even develop real health problems at a young age.","note":"递进一句把危害推到底。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my opinion, the solution lies in better time management rather than stronger willpower alone.","note":"评论有新意：靠时间管理而不是硬拼意志力；lie in（在于）准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Finishing important tasks earlier and putting the phone away before bed can help students win back their nights and their health.","note":"两个动名词给出具体做法；win back（赢回）收尾有力量。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["On any night in a university dormitory, the lights of phone screens can be seen long after midnight. Staying up late has become a shared habit among college students, and it is quietly harming their health and study.","There are several reasons behind this habit. Heavy study tasks and part-time jobs take up the daytime, so students push their entertainment and social life into the night. Phones make the problem worse: one more video or one more game easily steals an hour without being noticed. The effects are serious. Students who sleep too little feel sleepy in class, remember less of what they learn, and become weak and anxious over time. Some even develop real health problems at a young age.","In my opinion, the solution lies in better time management rather than stronger willpower alone. Finishing important tasks earlier and putting the phone away before bed can help students win back their nights and their health."],"id":"health-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Staying up late has become a common habit among college students. Analyze the causes and effects of this phenomenon and give your advice in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"大学生熬夜成风","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"During exam weeks, libraries are full of students who study through the night, trading sleep and health for a few more marks.","note":"场景开头 + trade A for B（拿 A 换 B），一句把现象和代价都点明。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This raises a real question: is health more important than grades?","note":"冒号引出核心问题，观点类开头有力。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"My answer is yes, without hesitation.","note":"without hesitation（毫不犹豫）短句表态，干净利落。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Grades matter, but they are only one part of a long life, while health is the basis of everything.","note":"while 对比句把两者定位：部分 vs 基础，立意句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A student who ruins his body for high marks may win a scholarship today but lose the energy to enjoy success tomorrow.","note":"today / tomorrow 时间对比，代价算得长远。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, the trade is often a poor deal in itself: a tired brain learns slowly and remembers little, so sacrificing sleep usually lowers efficiency instead of raising scores.","note":"a poor deal（亏本买卖）比喻 + 事实拆解：熬夜反而降效，论证反打对方逻辑。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Wise students plan their time so that study and rest support each other, and their results are no worse in the end.","note":"so that 目的从句；support each other 点出健康与成绩可以共赢。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, grades are the fruit, but health is the root.","note":"fruit / root 比喻对仗，全篇点睛句，值得背。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Only by protecting the root can we enjoy the fruit for a lifetime.","note":"Only by…can we… 倒装收尾，呼应比喻，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["During exam weeks, libraries are full of students who study through the night, trading sleep and health for a few more marks. This raises a real question: is health more important than grades? My answer is yes, without hesitation.","Grades matter, but they are only one part of a long life, while health is the basis of everything. A student who ruins his body for high marks may win a scholarship today but lose the energy to enjoy success tomorrow. Besides, the trade is often a poor deal in itself: a tired brain learns slowly and remembers little, so sacrificing sleep usually lowers efficiency instead of raising scores. Wise students plan their time so that study and rest support each other, and their results are no worse in the end.","In conclusion, grades are the fruit, but health is the root. Only by protecting the root can we enjoy the fruit for a lifetime."],"id":"health-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some students sacrifice sleep and exercise to get better grades. Do you think health is more important than grades? Write 120–180 words to state your opinion.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"健康比成绩更重要吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Faced with heavy study tasks, some students give up exercise completely, believing that every minute should be spent on books.","note":"分词短语开头摆出对方做法，背景一句交代完。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I hold the opposite view: daily exercise is not a waste of time but an investment in both health and study.","note":"hold the view 表态；not a waste but an investment（不是浪费而是投资）对比立意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To begin with, exercise keeps the body strong and the mind clear.","note":"理由一主题句：身体和头脑两头都点到。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"After an hour of running or ball games, students return to their desks with fresh energy, and their learning efficiency is often higher than before.","note":"用一个具体场景论证「运动反提效率」，回应了对方的核心担忧。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, regular exercise is one of the best ways to relieve stress.","note":"relieve stress（缓解压力）是健康主题必备搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Many students feel anxious before exams, and a good sweat helps them sleep better and face pressure with a calmer mind.","note":"a good sweat（一场痛快的出汗）说法鲜活；face pressure with a calmer mind 收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Of course, exercise should be kept at a reasonable level; training too hard or too long would leave students too tired to study.","note":"让步一句限定边界，观点不走极端。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In short, health and study are not enemies.","note":"短句比喻收尾：健康和学习不是敌人，一句点题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Half an hour of exercise a day buys back far more than it costs.","note":"buys back / costs 用买卖作比，和首段 investment 呼应，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Faced with heavy study tasks, some students give up exercise completely, believing that every minute should be spent on books. I hold the opposite view: daily exercise is not a waste of time but an investment in both health and study.","To begin with, exercise keeps the body strong and the mind clear. After an hour of running or ball games, students return to their desks with fresh energy, and their learning efficiency is often higher than before. Besides, regular exercise is one of the best ways to relieve stress. Many students feel anxious before exams, and a good sweat helps them sleep better and face pressure with a calmer mind. Of course, exercise should be kept at a reasonable level; training too hard or too long would leave students too tired to study.","In short, health and study are not enemies. Half an hour of exercise a day buys back far more than it costs."],"id":"health-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some students believe daily exercise is a waste of study time, while others insist on exercising every day. What is your opinion? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"大学生要不要每天运动","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"With a few taps on the phone, a hot meal arrives at the dormitory door.","note":"With 短语 + 一个动作画面开头，外卖的便利不用形容就出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Takeaway food has become the first choice of many college students, but eating it too often is a habit worth thinking about.","note":"先肯定现象再埋下转折，worth thinking about 引出利弊分析。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The advantages are easy to see.","note":"短句开启正面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Takeaway food is convenient and time-saving, which matters a lot to students busy with classes and activities.","note":"time-saving 复合形容词；which 从句补一句「对谁重要」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"It also offers rich choices, from local snacks to dishes from faraway places.","note":"from…to… 句式把「选择丰富」写具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, the disadvantages are serious.","note":"转折短句开启负面段，定调明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Much takeaway food is high in oil, salt and sugar, and eating it day after day may lead to weight gain and stomach problems.","note":"be high in（富含）、lead to（导致）都是健康话题准搭配；day after day 强调频率。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Food safety is another concern, since we cannot see how the food is prepared.","note":"another concern 换角度；since 从句给出看不见后厨的具体理由。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, the cost adds up quietly: a month of takeaway meals may equal a whole term of canteen dinners.","note":"adds up（累积起来）+ 一个具体对比算账，坏处写得扎实。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, takeaway food is fine once in a while, but the canteen should remain our main dining place.","note":"once in a while（偶尔）限定频率，结论有分寸、不一刀切。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Convenience is sweet, but health is priceless.","note":"对仗短句收尾：便利虽甜，健康无价——好背好套。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["With a few taps on the phone, a hot meal arrives at the dormitory door. Takeaway food has become the first choice of many college students, but eating it too often is a habit worth thinking about.","The advantages are easy to see. Takeaway food is convenient and time-saving, which matters a lot to students busy with classes and activities. It also offers rich choices, from local snacks to dishes from faraway places. However, the disadvantages are serious. Much takeaway food is high in oil, salt and sugar, and eating it day after day may lead to weight gain and stomach problems. Food safety is another concern, since we cannot see how the food is prepared. Besides, the cost adds up quietly: a month of takeaway meals may equal a whole term of canteen dinners.","In my view, takeaway food is fine once in a while, but the canteen should remain our main dining place. Convenience is sweet, but health is priceless."],"id":"health-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Ordering takeaway food has become a daily habit for many college students. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of eating takeaway food frequently in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"天天点外卖","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"A typical day for many college students is spent almost entirely in a chair: lectures in the morning, homework in the library, and games or videos in the dormitory at night.","note":"冒号后三个场景并列，一天「坐穿」的生活一目了然。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Sitting for ten hours a day has quietly become the norm, and it is doing real harm.","note":"become the norm（成为常态）准说法；doing real harm 点明问题。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The risks should not be underestimated.","note":"被动句开启危害段，语气正式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Sitting too long slows blood circulation, causes pain in the neck and back, and raises the risk of gaining weight and other diseases over time.","note":"三个动词并列列危害；blood circulation（血液循环）用词准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It also makes people feel tired and low in spirits, even though they have done little physical work.","note":"low in spirits（没精神）；even though 让步点出「没干活却累」的反常感。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To change this, small moves are the most realistic answer.","note":"对策段先给总思路：小动作——务实，不喊大口号。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students can stand up and walk around for a few minutes after every hour of study, choose stairs instead of lifts, and walk or cycle to places that are not far.","note":"三条小建议并列，全是今天就能做的事，建议的可执行性就是分。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Scheduling two or three exercise sessions a week also helps the body recover from long sitting.","note":"recover from（从……恢复）搭配准确。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In short, we cannot avoid sitting as students, but we can break it up.","note":"break it up（把久坐打断）说法地道，结论先认现实再给办法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Moving a little, often, is the simplest medicine.","note":"medicine 比喻收尾：动一点、常动，就是最简单的药。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["A typical day for many college students is spent almost entirely in a chair: lectures in the morning, homework in the library, and games or videos in the dormitory at night. Sitting for ten hours a day has quietly become the norm, and it is doing real harm.","The risks should not be underestimated. Sitting too long slows blood circulation, causes pain in the neck and back, and raises the risk of gaining weight and other diseases over time. It also makes people feel tired and low in spirits, even though they have done little physical work. To change this, small moves are the most realistic answer. Students can stand up and walk around for a few minutes after every hour of study, choose stairs instead of lifts, and walk or cycle to places that are not far. Scheduling two or three exercise sessions a week also helps the body recover from long sitting.","In short, we cannot avoid sitting as students, but we can break it up. Moving a little, often, is the simplest medicine."],"id":"health-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many college students sit for most of the day — in classrooms, libraries and dormitories — and seldom move around. What are the risks of sitting too long, and how can students change this? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"久坐不动的大学生","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear fellow students,","note":"倡议书称呼，对象明确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"University life is full of chances, but also full of pressure.","note":"对仗句开头：机会与压力并存，把话题立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Exams, relationships and worries about the future sometimes make us anxious, tired or even helpless.","note":"三个压力来源 + 三个感受形容词并列，心理话题的词汇密度一下上来。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Mental health is as important as physical health, and it deserves our serious attention.","note":"as important as 对比两个健康，点明倡议的立意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To help everyone face pressure in a healthier way, the Students' Union will hold a Mental Health Week next week and proposes the following.","note":"交代活动 + proposes the following 引出分点，倡议书标准结构。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, take part in the activities actively.","note":"倡议分点：先号召参与，主题句简洁。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"There will be lectures by psychologists, group games on the playground and a hotline where you can talk about your troubles freely.","note":"三个活动并列写具体；hotline（热线）+ where 从句，信息完整。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, learn to care for your own feelings in daily life: keep a regular schedule, exercise, and share your worries with friends instead of keeping everything inside.","note":"冒号后三条日常做法；instead of keeping everything inside（而不是全憋在心里）写得体贴。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Third, care for the people around you.","note":"第三条从「自己」推到「他人」，倡议有层次。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A warm word at the right moment may mean a lot to a classmate in trouble.","note":"mean a lot（意义重大）收束第三点，温情落点。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Let us join hands to build a campus where everyone feels supported and understood.","note":"join hands（携手）+ where 从句展望，落款 The Students' Union，格式完整。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear fellow students,","University life is full of chances, but also full of pressure. Exams, relationships and worries about the future sometimes make us anxious, tired or even helpless. Mental health is as important as physical health, and it deserves our serious attention. To help everyone face pressure in a healthier way, the Students' Union will hold a Mental Health Week next week and proposes the following.","First, take part in the activities actively. There will be lectures by psychologists, group games on the playground and a hotline where you can talk about your troubles freely. Second, learn to care for your own feelings in daily life: keep a regular schedule, exercise, and share your worries with friends instead of keeping everything inside. Third, care for the people around you. A warm word at the right moment may mean a lot to a classmate in trouble.","Let us join hands to build a campus where everyone feels supported and understood.","The Students' Union"],"id":"health-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Your university is going to hold a Mental Health Week. As a member of the Students' Union, write a proposal (倡议书) of 120–180 words calling on students to pay attention to mental health and join the activities.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"倡议书：心理健康周","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Most college students feel young and strong, so a physical examination seems unnecessary to them; many have not had one since entering university.","note":"分号连接两层现象，physical examination（体检）关键词先亮出来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my opinion, a yearly physical examination is necessary and worth both the time and the money.","note":"be worth（值得）表态，提前回应「费时费钱」的质疑。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To begin with, many health problems show no clear signs at an early stage.","note":"理由一：早期无症状——at an early stage 准词组。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"High blood pressure, poor eyesight and stomach trouble can develop silently for years, and an examination is often the only way to discover them in time.","note":"三个具体病症并列；in time（及时）点出体检的核心价值。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, an examination report is a useful reminder about lifestyle.","note":"理由二换角度：体检报告是生活方式的提醒，立意比「查病」更进一层。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When students see their weight, sleep or eyesight getting worse in black and white, they are more willing to change bad habits than when teachers simply tell them to.","note":"in black and white（白纸黑字）形象；两个 when 从句对比，说服力强。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Admittedly, examinations cost money, but treating a serious illness costs far more, both in money and in health.","note":"Admittedly 让步 + 算账对比：小钱 vs 大钱大病，让步反成论据。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, youth is not a promise of health.","note":"短句格言式收尾：年轻不是健康的保证。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A yearly check is a small price for early warning and peace of mind.","note":"peace of mind（安心）收尾，把体检的价值落在「预警 + 安心」。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Most college students feel young and strong, so a physical examination seems unnecessary to them; many have not had one since entering university. In my opinion, a yearly physical examination is necessary and worth both the time and the money.","To begin with, many health problems show no clear signs at an early stage. High blood pressure, poor eyesight and stomach trouble can develop silently for years, and an examination is often the only way to discover them in time. Besides, an examination report is a useful reminder about lifestyle. When students see their weight, sleep or eyesight getting worse in black and white, they are more willing to change bad habits than when teachers simply tell them to. Admittedly, examinations cost money, but treating a serious illness costs far more, both in money and in health.","In conclusion, youth is not a promise of health. A yearly check is a small price for early warning and peace of mind."],"id":"health-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many young people never have a physical examination unless they feel sick. Do you think a yearly physical examination is necessary for college students? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"体检该不该每年做","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Look around any classroom today and you will find that most students wear glasses.","note":"祈使句带读者环顾教室，现象一秒入画。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Poor eyesight has become so common among young people that it is now a public health concern rather than a personal matter.","note":"so…that… + rather than 把问题从个人拔高到公共健康，立意升级。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The causes are closely related to modern study life.","note":"原因段总起：be closely related to（与……密切相关）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Students spend long hours reading and writing with their eyes close to books, and in their free time they turn to phones and computers instead of resting their eyes.","note":"学习时和休息时两个场景并列，近视的原因全在「眼睛没得歇」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Outdoor activities, which are natural protection for eyesight, have been squeezed out by heavy homework and electronic entertainment.","note":"be squeezed out（被挤掉）形象；which 从句点出户外活动的护眼作用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To protect our eyes, several habits matter.","note":"对策段总起短句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"We should rest our eyes regularly during study, keep a proper distance from books and screens, and spend more time outdoors every day.","note":"三条习惯并列；keep a proper distance（保持适当距离）是护眼话题准说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Schools should also make eye exercises and physical activities a real part of the daily schedule, not a formality.","note":"not a formality（不是走形式）一句点出关键，建议有洞察。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Eyesight, once lost, is hard to get back.","note":"once lost 分词短语，短句警示收尾。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Protecting it should begin today, not tomorrow.","note":"today / tomorrow 对比收尾，行动感强，好背好套。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Look around any classroom today and you will find that most students wear glasses. Poor eyesight has become so common among young people that it is now a public health concern rather than a personal matter.","The causes are closely related to modern study life. Students spend long hours reading and writing with their eyes close to books, and in their free time they turn to phones and computers instead of resting their eyes. Outdoor activities, which are natural protection for eyesight, have been squeezed out by heavy homework and electronic entertainment. To protect our eyes, several habits matter. We should rest our eyes regularly during study, keep a proper distance from books and screens, and spend more time outdoors every day. Schools should also make eye exercises and physical activities a real part of the daily schedule, not a formality.","Eyesight, once lost, is hard to get back. Protecting it should begin today, not tomorrow."],"id":"health-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: More and more students wear glasses today, and many start wearing them at a very young age. Analyze the causes of this phenomenon and suggest ways to protect eyesight in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"近视越来越低龄、越来越普遍","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"During exam weeks, cans of energy drinks and cups of strong coffee appear on almost every desk in the library.","note":"场景细节开头：图书馆桌上的罐子和杯子，现象立现。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Students depend on them to fight sleepiness, but is this habit really helpful?","note":"结尾一个问句引出利弊讨论，开头有钩子。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the positive side, these drinks do work in the short term.","note":"On the positive side 开启正面；in the short term（短期内）埋下转折伏笔；do work 的 do 表强调。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Caffeine makes people feel more awake and focused, helping them finish urgent tasks or survive an important exam morning.","note":"caffeine（咖啡因）用词准确；survive an exam morning 说法鲜活。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For a busy night before a deadline, they seem like a quick rescue.","note":"a quick rescue（快速救援）比喻，正面段收得形象。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, the cost is paid later.","note":"短句转折：代价随后就来——节奏一顿，印象深刻。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Too much caffeine disturbs sleep, so students feel even more tired the next day and need even more drinks, falling into a bad circle.","note":"因果链一路推下去；fall into a bad circle（陷入恶性循环）是点睛词组。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Over time, depending on such drinks may harm the heart and stomach, and the real problem — poor time management — is never solved.","note":"破折号插入语点出真问题：不是困，是时间管理差——分析深一层。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, an energy drink is acceptable in a real emergency, but it should never become a daily habit.","note":"结论分寸感：急救可以，日常不行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Regular sleep is the only healthy way to stay energetic.","note":"stay energetic（保持精力充沛）收尾扣题。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["During exam weeks, cans of energy drinks and cups of strong coffee appear on almost every desk in the library. Students depend on them to fight sleepiness, but is this habit really helpful?","On the positive side, these drinks do work in the short term. Caffeine makes people feel more awake and focused, helping them finish urgent tasks or survive an important exam morning. For a busy night before a deadline, they seem like a quick rescue. However, the cost is paid later. Too much caffeine disturbs sleep, so students feel even more tired the next day and need even more drinks, falling into a bad circle. Over time, depending on such drinks may harm the heart and stomach, and the real problem — poor time management — is never solved.","In my view, an energy drink is acceptable in a real emergency, but it should never become a daily habit. Regular sleep is the only healthy way to stay energetic."],"id":"health-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many students drink energy drinks or strong coffee to stay awake during exam weeks. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this habit in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"喝功能饮料提神","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Beneath the lively surface of campus life, many college students are quietly struggling with psychological pressure.","note":"Beneath the surface（表面之下）开头，对比出问题的隐蔽性。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some lose sleep over exams, some feel lost about the future, and a few develop more serious mental problems.","note":"some…some…a few… 三层递进，人群和程度都写清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The pressure comes from several directions.","note":"原因段总起句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Study and competition are the most obvious sources: students compare themselves with excellent classmates and fear falling behind.","note":"compare oneself with（和……比较）、fall behind 都是压力话题准词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Worries about jobs after graduation add another heavy stone, especially in the final years.","note":"add another heavy stone 比喻形象，把就业压力具体化。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, being away from family for the first time, many students keep their troubles to themselves instead of seeking support.","note":"keep troubles to oneself（把烦恼憋在心里）与 seeking support 对比，点出关键误区。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To deal with the pressure, students should first accept that feeling stressed is normal and not a weakness.","note":"对策第一条先讲观念：压力正常、不是软弱——顺序安排有见识。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Talking to friends, teachers or school counselors can release much of the burden, and regular exercise and hobbies help the mind recover.","note":"release the burden（卸下负担）、counselors（心理咨询师）用词准确。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When pressure becomes too heavy to bear, asking professionals for help is a wise and brave choice.","note":"too…to… 句式；wise and brave 重新定义「求助」，立意加分。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, mental health problems should be faced, not hidden.","note":"faced, not hidden 对仗收尾主张。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Seeking help in time is the first step toward feeling better.","note":"动名词作主语收尾，落点积极可操作。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Beneath the lively surface of campus life, many college students are quietly struggling with psychological pressure. Some lose sleep over exams, some feel lost about the future, and a few develop more serious mental problems.","The pressure comes from several directions. Study and competition are the most obvious sources: students compare themselves with excellent classmates and fear falling behind. Worries about jobs after graduation add another heavy stone, especially in the final years. Besides, being away from family for the first time, many students keep their troubles to themselves instead of seeking support. To deal with the pressure, students should first accept that feeling stressed is normal and not a weakness. Talking to friends, teachers or school counselors can release much of the burden, and regular exercise and hobbies help the mind recover. When pressure becomes too heavy to bear, asking professionals for help is a wise and brave choice.","In short, mental health problems should be faced, not hidden. Seeking help in time is the first step toward feeling better."],"id":"health-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many college students suffer from psychological pressure and some even develop mental health problems. What causes the pressure, and how should students deal with it? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"health","themeName":"健康","title":"大学生心理压力大","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Star-chasing is no longer a small hobby for a few fans.","note":"no longer（不再是）一句点出现象规模变大，现象类好开头。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many young people today spend hours every day following news about their idols, buying related products and voting online to support them.","note":"三个动名词并列把追星的日常写具体，不空泛。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Several factors explain the popularity of this phenomenon.","note":"原因段总起句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Idols are usually young, good-looking and talented, and their hard-working image gives fans energy and hope in daily life.","note":"三个形容词并列描偶像；image（形象）用词准确。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Social media makes the distance between idols and fans seem much shorter, so fans feel emotionally close to the stars they support.","note":"emotionally close（情感上亲近）点出社交媒体的作用机制，分析有深度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, star-chasing can go too far.","note":"go too far（过头）短句转折，开启问题面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some fans spend money far beyond their means, copy their idols' words without thinking, or even attack others online in the name of love.","note":"beyond their means（超出经济能力）准词组；三个行为递进，最后 in the name of love 一针见血。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, admiring an idol is natural and can be positive when it encourages young people to improve themselves.","note":"评论先肯定合理性，when 从句给出「积极」的条件。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The key is to stay rational: learn from the idol's strengths, but never lose your own life and judgment.","note":"冒号展开「理性」的含义；judgment（判断力）收尾，落点成熟。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Star-chasing is no longer a small hobby for a few fans. Many young people today spend hours every day following news about their idols, buying related products and voting online to support them.","Several factors explain the popularity of this phenomenon. Idols are usually young, good-looking and talented, and their hard-working image gives fans energy and hope in daily life. Social media makes the distance between idols and fans seem much shorter, so fans feel emotionally close to the stars they support. However, star-chasing can go too far. Some fans spend money far beyond their means, copy their idols' words without thinking, or even attack others online in the name of love.","In my view, admiring an idol is natural and can be positive when it encourages young people to improve themselves. The key is to stay rational: learn from the idol's strengths, but never lose your own life and judgment."],"id":"soc-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many young people spend a lot of time and money following their idols. Analyze this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"追星文化","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Second-hand platforms are booming.","note":"短句开篇，booming（蓬勃兴起）一个词点明热度。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On these apps, students sell textbooks they no longer need, buy phones at half price, and exchange almost everything, from bicycles to concert tickets.","note":"三个动词并列 + from…to…，平台上的交易画面全出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The advantages are clear.","note":"短句开启正面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For buyers, second-hand goods cost much less, which is especially friendly to students with limited budgets.","note":"For buyers / For sellers 对称开启两方好处；limited budgets（预算有限）准说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"For sellers, idle things at home turn into money instead of rubbish.","note":"turn into money instead of rubbish 对比，闲置变废为宝一句说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"More importantly, reusing goods saves resources and reduces waste, making this trend good for the environment as well.","note":"Most importantly 式递进：从省钱升到环保，好处有层次。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, disadvantages exist.","note":"最简转折短句，开启负面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The quality of second-hand goods cannot always be trusted; photos may hide faults, and returning goods is often troublesome.","note":"分号展开两个具体麻烦：照片藏瑕疵、退货难。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Cheating happens from time to time, and buyers have weaker protection than in normal shops.","note":"from time to time（时有发生）；weaker protection 点出制度层面的短板。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, second-hand trading is a smart and green way of consumption, as long as platforms keep strict rules and buyers stay careful.","note":"结论带 as long as 条件：平台管好、人小心，判断有分寸。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Used wisely, yesterday's goods can begin a second life in new hands.","note":"a second life（第二次生命）比喻收尾，与 second-hand 呼应，巧。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Second-hand platforms are booming. On these apps, students sell textbooks they no longer need, buy phones at half price, and exchange almost everything, from bicycles to concert tickets.","The advantages are clear. For buyers, second-hand goods cost much less, which is especially friendly to students with limited budgets. For sellers, idle things at home turn into money instead of rubbish. More importantly, reusing goods saves resources and reduces waste, making this trend good for the environment as well. However, disadvantages exist. The quality of second-hand goods cannot always be trusted; photos may hide faults, and returning goods is often troublesome. Cheating happens from time to time, and buyers have weaker protection than in normal shops.","In conclusion, second-hand trading is a smart and green way of consumption, as long as platforms keep strict rules and buyers stay careful. Used wisely, yesterday's goods can begin a second life in new hands."],"id":"soc-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Buying and selling second-hand goods on online platforms has become popular among young people. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this trend in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"二手交易流行","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"It is not rare today to see young graduates who still ask their parents for money to pay rent or buy what they want.","note":"It is not rare to see… 用双重否定描述现象，具体到付房租。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, depending on parents in an emergency is acceptable, but adults should become financially independent as early as possible.","note":"表态带限定：应急可以、长期不行；financially independent（经济独立）是本题关键词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, independence is a necessary step in growing up.","note":"理由一主题句：独立是成长的必经一步。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A person who earns his own living learns to plan, to save and to take responsibility for his choices — lessons no classroom can teach as deeply.","note":"三个 to do 并列 + 破折号补评语；earn one's living（谋生）准词组。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, depending on parents places a heavy burden on them.","note":"place a burden on（给……增加负担）正式搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Most parents have worked hard for decades and deserve a relaxed life in their later years, not another mouth to feed.","note":"another mouth to feed（多一张要养的嘴）说法形象，理由落到父母身上，有温度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Admittedly, the first years after graduation are difficult, and temporary help from parents can be a warm support.","note":"Admittedly 让步，承认起步难。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"But such help should be a bridge, not a home.","note":"bridge / home 比喻对仗：帮助是桥不是家——全篇点睛句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, standing on one's own feet is both a duty to parents and a gift to oneself.","note":"stand on one's own feet（自立）成语用对；both… 两个角度收束。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The earlier young people achieve it, the more confident they will be in life.","note":"The earlier…, the more… 句式收尾，越早独立越自信。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["It is not rare today to see young graduates who still ask their parents for money to pay rent or buy what they want. In my view, depending on parents in an emergency is acceptable, but adults should become financially independent as early as possible.","To begin with, independence is a necessary step in growing up. A person who earns his own living learns to plan, to save and to take responsibility for his choices — lessons no classroom can teach as deeply. Besides, depending on parents places a heavy burden on them. Most parents have worked hard for decades and deserve a relaxed life in their later years, not another mouth to feed. Admittedly, the first years after graduation are difficult, and temporary help from parents can be a warm support. But such help should be a bridge, not a home.","In conclusion, standing on one's own feet is both a duty to parents and a gift to oneself. The earlier young people achieve it, the more confident they will be in life."],"id":"soc-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some young people still depend on their parents for money after graduating from university. Do you think adults should be financially independent? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"成年后该不该靠父母","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Sending money gifts to live-stream hosts has become a common way for viewers to show support.","note":"动名词作主语开篇，现象一句说清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A small red packet or a virtual gift lights up the screen, and the host thanks the sender by name.","note":"一个具体画面解释打赏是怎么回事，照顾不熟悉这个现象的读者（阅卷人）。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This practice has both a bright side and a dark side.","note":"bright side / dark side 预告利弊，比 advantages/disadvantages 更活。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the bright side, tipping is a voluntary way to pay for entertainment one enjoys, much like buying a ticket for a concert.","note":"类比演唱会门票，把打赏的合理性讲得通俗；voluntary（自愿的）是关键词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"It encourages hosts to produce better content and allows talented ordinary people to earn a living by their skills.","note":"earn a living by（靠……谋生）准搭配；好处落到普通人身上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On the dark side, however, the system is designed to excite emotions.","note":"与 bright side 成对转折；is designed to 点出机制设计，分析深一层。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Rankings and competitions push viewers to give more than they planned, and some young people have spent their family's savings or even borrowed money to tip.","note":"从「比计划多」递进到「花掉积蓄、借钱」，危害层层加码。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What begins as support can end as addiction.","note":"what 主语从句 + support/addiction 对比，短句点睛。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, tipping should stay a small pleasure within one's means.","note":"within one's means（量力而行）是消费类话题的万能落点词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Platforms should also set limits, especially to protect young viewers from spending beyond control.","note":"结论补上平台责任，protect sb from（保护某人免于）收尾。","tag":"好词"}],"essay":["Sending money gifts to live-stream hosts has become a common way for viewers to show support. A small red packet or a virtual gift lights up the screen, and the host thanks the sender by name. This practice has both a bright side and a dark side.","On the bright side, tipping is a voluntary way to pay for entertainment one enjoys, much like buying a ticket for a concert. It encourages hosts to produce better content and allows talented ordinary people to earn a living by their skills. On the dark side, however, the system is designed to excite emotions. Rankings and competitions push viewers to give more than they planned, and some young people have spent their family's savings or even borrowed money to tip. What begins as support can end as addiction.","In my opinion, tipping should stay a small pleasure within one's means. Platforms should also set limits, especially to protect young viewers from spending beyond control."],"id":"soc-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many viewers send money gifts (打赏) to live-stream hosts, and some spend far more than they can afford. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this practice in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"给主播打赏","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Scanning a code to pay, booking a doctor online, showing a health code to travel — daily life today is built on smartphones.","note":"三个动名词排比摆出「处处要手机」的日常，开头代入感强。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"For many elderly people, however, these simple actions are high walls, and being left behind by technology makes them feel helpless.","note":"high walls 比喻 + be left behind（被落下），问题写得有共情；the elderly 是「老人」的正式说法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Solving this problem requires efforts from several sides.","note":"对策段总起：多方努力，预告三条分工。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, technology should become friendlier to older users.","note":"第一条先给定位：让技术适应老人，而不是只让老人追赶技术。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Apps can offer a senior mode with larger words, simpler pages and voice guidance, so that learning becomes less frightening.","note":"senior mode（长辈模式）是真实存在的说法；三个名词并列写具体功能。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, families should teach patiently.","note":"第二条换主体到家庭，短句主题句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Young people can show their parents step by step and write down the steps, instead of simply doing everything for them.","note":"step by step + instead of doing everything for them：教方法而非代劳，建议有洞察。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Third, public services must keep traditional choices: a window where the elderly can pay in cash and ask a real person should never disappear completely.","note":"第三条落到公共服务保留线下窗口；where 定语从句把「窗口」写具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, a truly advanced society is not one that runs fastest, but one that is willing to slow down and wait for its elderly members.","note":"not one that…but one that… 对比收尾：先进不在于跑得快，而在于愿意等——全篇立意最高的一句。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Scanning a code to pay, booking a doctor online, showing a health code to travel — daily life today is built on smartphones. For many elderly people, however, these simple actions are high walls, and being left behind by technology makes them feel helpless.","Solving this problem requires efforts from several sides. First, technology should become friendlier to older users. Apps can offer a senior mode with larger words, simpler pages and voice guidance, so that learning becomes less frightening. Second, families should teach patiently. Young people can show their parents step by step and write down the steps, instead of simply doing everything for them. Third, public services must keep traditional choices: a window where the elderly can pay in cash and ask a real person should never disappear completely.","In short, a truly advanced society is not one that runs fastest, but one that is willing to slow down and wait for its elderly members."],"id":"soc-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many elderly people find it hard to use smartphones, which causes difficulties in paying, seeing doctors and traveling. How can this problem be solved? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"老年人不会用智能手机","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Every year, the civil service examination attracts millions of applicants, and for some positions, thousands of graduates compete for a single post.","note":"用「数千人争一个岗位」的数字画面开篇，现象的热度不用形容。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The fever for government jobs has become a notable social phenomenon.","note":"fever（热潮）比喻；social phenomenon 是本题主题词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The reasons are not hard to find.","note":"短句开启原因段，过渡自然。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Most importantly, a civil service job means stability: a steady income, regular hours and good social security, which are especially attractive when the job market is uncertain.","note":"冒号列出「稳定」的三层含义；social security（社保）准词；when 从句点出大环境。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, such jobs carry social respect, and many parents regard them as the best choice for their children.","note":"第二条原因落到社会观念和父母期待，regard A as B 句型好用。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"However, the fever also has a worrying side.","note":"转折短句开启担忧面，评论不一边倒。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"When too many talented young people spend years preparing for one examination, much creativity and energy is locked in waiting rooms.","note":"locked in waiting rooms 比喻：才华被锁在备考里，画面感强。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Those who fail repeatedly may lose precious years that could have been spent building other careers.","note":"两个定语从句叠加，代价说得具体：输掉的是几年时间。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, a government job is a respectable choice, but it is only one road among many.","note":"评论先肯定再限定，one road among many 落点稳。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Young people should choose based on their own interests and abilities, not simply on what looks safest.","note":"based on…not on… 对比收尾，建议指向独立判断。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Every year, the civil service examination attracts millions of applicants, and for some positions, thousands of graduates compete for a single post. The fever for government jobs has become a notable social phenomenon.","The reasons are not hard to find. Most importantly, a civil service job means stability: a steady income, regular hours and good social security, which are especially attractive when the job market is uncertain. Besides, such jobs carry social respect, and many parents regard them as the best choice for their children. However, the fever also has a worrying side. When too many talented young people spend years preparing for one examination, much creativity and energy is locked in waiting rooms. Those who fail repeatedly may lose precious years that could have been spent building other careers.","In my view, a government job is a respectable choice, but it is only one road among many. Young people should choose based on their own interests and abilities, not simply on what looks safest."],"id":"soc-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: In recent years, applying for civil service jobs has become extremely popular among graduates, with thousands competing for a single position. Analyze the reasons and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"考公热","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In the early morning and evening, music rises from squares and parks as groups of elderly people dance together happily.","note":"场景开头：时间 + 音乐 + 人群，现象如在眼前。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Square dancing keeps them healthy and cheerful, yet the loud music has also become a source of conflict with nearby residents who need quiet rest.","note":"yet 一句摆出矛盾双方，问题解决型的好开头：先讲清冲突。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The conflict exists because both sides have reasonable needs.","note":"分析段先定调：双方都有理——这是解决冲突类题目的立意关键。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The elderly deserve places to exercise and enjoy their later life, while residents who work all day deserve a quiet home.","note":"deserve 两次并列，两边的正当性对称地摆出来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The key is not to choose a winner but to find rules both sides can accept.","note":"not to…but to… 点出解法方向：定规则，不分胜负。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Communities can set fixed places and hours for dancing, keeping it away from bedroom windows and ending it before rest time.","note":"对策具体到地点和时间；keep it away from 细节真实。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Dancing groups can lower the volume or use shared earphones, a method already welcomed in some cities.","note":"补一个真实存在的新办法（静音广场舞耳机），建议有新意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Residents, for their part, can show more understanding, since today's dancers are tomorrow's elderly — perhaps including ourselves.","note":"for their part（就居民而言）分工完整；最后一句换位思考，有温度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, a little consideration from each side can turn a noisy argument into a friendly neighborhood.","note":"turn…into… 收尾：把争吵变邻里和气，全文落点。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In the early morning and evening, music rises from squares and parks as groups of elderly people dance together happily. Square dancing keeps them healthy and cheerful, yet the loud music has also become a source of conflict with nearby residents who need quiet rest.","The conflict exists because both sides have reasonable needs. The elderly deserve places to exercise and enjoy their later life, while residents who work all day deserve a quiet home. The key is not to choose a winner but to find rules both sides can accept. Communities can set fixed places and hours for dancing, keeping it away from bedroom windows and ending it before rest time. Dancing groups can lower the volume or use shared earphones, a method already welcomed in some cities. Residents, for their part, can show more understanding, since today's dancers are tomorrow's elderly — perhaps including ourselves.","In short, a little consideration from each side can turn a noisy argument into a friendly neighborhood."],"id":"soc-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Square dancing is popular among elderly people, but its loud music often disturbs nearby residents. How can this conflict be solved? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"广场舞扰民","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Helping a fallen elderly person used to be a natural act of kindness.","note":"used to be（过去是）开头，与今天形成对比，问题自然浮现。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today, however, some people walk past with hesitation, fearing that their kindness may be repaid with blame.","note":"be repaid with blame（善意被指责回报）说法精准，一句写尽纠结。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This change is sad, but the answer is not to stop helping.","note":"第一段就表态：难过，但不能不扶——观点类要的就是这个明确劲儿。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Fear has its reasons.","note":"短句开启分析：先承认恐惧有来由，文章不站着说话不腰疼。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A few dishonest people have indeed cheated kind helpers, and such news, widely spread online, makes everyone more careful.","note":"indeed 承让步；widely spread online 点出新闻放大效应，分析到位。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"But these cases are rare compared with the countless true acts of help given every day.","note":"rare ↔ countless 对比，用比例感把恐惧拉回理性。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"If everyone chooses to look away, an elderly person lying on the ground may miss the best time for treatment, and society will grow cold.","note":"if 条件句推演后果：从个人安危推到社会变冷，层层递进。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In fact, helpers today can protect themselves while helping: asking others to witness, recording the scene, or calling the police first are all practical ways.","note":"冒号后三条自保办法并列，建议落地——观点类有对策才完整。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, kindness should not be defeated by fear.","note":"be defeated by（被打败）拟人收尾主张，短句有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A society where people dare to help is the kind of society we all want to live in.","note":"where 定语从句收尾展望，dare to help（敢扶）扣回题目。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Helping a fallen elderly person used to be a natural act of kindness. Today, however, some people walk past with hesitation, fearing that their kindness may be repaid with blame. This change is sad, but the answer is not to stop helping.","Fear has its reasons. A few dishonest people have indeed cheated kind helpers, and such news, widely spread online, makes everyone more careful. But these cases are rare compared with the countless true acts of help given every day. If everyone chooses to look away, an elderly person lying on the ground may miss the best time for treatment, and society will grow cold. In fact, helpers today can protect themselves while helping: asking others to witness, recording the scene, or calling the police first are all practical ways.","In conclusion, kindness should not be defeated by fear. A society where people dare to help is the kind of society we all want to live in."],"id":"soc-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people hesitate to help an elderly person who has fallen down, worrying about being wrongly blamed. What is your view on this social problem? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"该不该扶摔倒的老人","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear fellow tourists,","note":"倡议书称呼锁定对象：游客。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Travel is a chance to enjoy beautiful scenery and rich culture.","note":"先肯定旅游的美好，倡议书先扬后批，语气不冲。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"However, during every holiday, news reports show uncivilized behavior: rubbish left on beaches, names carved on ancient walls, and loud voices in quiet museums.","note":"冒号后三个具体画面列举不文明行为，比抽象批评有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Such behavior damages both the scenery and the image of all tourists.","note":"damage the image（损害形象）点出危害的第二层。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To make every journey pleasant, we propose the following.","note":"propose the following 倡议书标志句，引出分点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, take your rubbish with you and leave every place as clean as you found it.","note":"leave…as clean as you found it（离开时和来时一样干净）说法地道好记。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Second, respect local rules and customs: queue in order, keep quiet in public places, and never touch or carve on historic relics.","note":"historic relics（文物古迹）准词；三个祈使并列，倡议具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Third, be a good example to others, especially to children traveling with you, because behavior teaches more than words.","note":"behavior teaches more than words 一句格言味的话，第三点立意最高。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Civilized travel begins with each of us.","note":"收尾号召短句，倡议书的点睛句式。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Let us protect the beauty we come to see, so that it will still be there for those who come after us.","note":"so that 目的从句 + those who come after us（后来人），落款 A Group of Travel Lovers，格式完整。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Dear fellow tourists,","Travel is a chance to enjoy beautiful scenery and rich culture. However, during every holiday, news reports show uncivilized behavior: rubbish left on beaches, names carved on ancient walls, and loud voices in quiet museums. Such behavior damages both the scenery and the image of all tourists. To make every journey pleasant, we propose the following.","First, take your rubbish with you and leave every place as clean as you found it. Second, respect local rules and customs: queue in order, keep quiet in public places, and never touch or carve on historic relics. Third, be a good example to others, especially to children traveling with you, because behavior teaches more than words.","Civilized travel begins with each of us. Let us protect the beauty we come to see, so that it will still be there for those who come after us.","A Group of Travel Lovers"],"id":"soc-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Uncivilized behavior by tourists, such as littering and carving names on historic sites, is often reported during holidays. Write a proposal (倡议书) of 120–180 words calling on tourists to travel in a civilized way.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"倡议书：文明旅游","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In today's cities, pets are everywhere: dogs in parks, cats on social media, and pet shops on almost every street.","note":"冒号后三个画面并列，现象的普遍性不用数字也立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Keeping a pet, once seen as an old people's hobby, has become a fashion among the young.","note":"once seen as… 插入语对比今昔：从老人爱好到年轻人时尚。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The reasons lie in modern city life.","note":"lie in（根源在于）总起原因段，一句点出分析方向。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many young people live alone far from their families, and a pet offers warm company that eases loneliness after a long day of work.","note":"company 在这里是「陪伴」；ease loneliness（缓解孤独）点出情感需求。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Pets also bring simple and honest joy; unlike the pressure of human relationships, a dog's welcome at the door never changes.","note":"分号 + unlike 对比：一句写出宠物之于人的独特价值。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, rising incomes make the cost of food and medical care for pets affordable to more families.","note":"rising incomes 补经济原因；make…affordable to 句型好用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, keeping a pet is a long-term responsibility, not a short-term fashion.","note":"转折句点出问题面：long-term / short-term 对比。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Sadly, some pets are abandoned when their owners move, get busy or lose interest.","note":"be abandoned（被遗弃）被动句；三个 when 场景并列，问题具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my opinion, loving pets is a good thing, but adoption should come after careful thought.","note":"评论先肯定再提醒，adoption（领养/饲养决定）用词准。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A pet is a family member for over ten years, not a toy for a season.","note":"family member / toy 对比收尾，时间和情感的账一句话算清。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In today's cities, pets are everywhere: dogs in parks, cats on social media, and pet shops on almost every street. Keeping a pet, once seen as an old people's hobby, has become a fashion among the young.","The reasons lie in modern city life. Many young people live alone far from their families, and a pet offers warm company that eases loneliness after a long day of work. Pets also bring simple and honest joy; unlike the pressure of human relationships, a dog's welcome at the door never changes. Besides, rising incomes make the cost of food and medical care for pets affordable to more families. However, keeping a pet is a long-term responsibility, not a short-term fashion. Sadly, some pets are abandoned when their owners move, get busy or lose interest.","In my opinion, loving pets is a good thing, but adoption should come after careful thought. A pet is a family member for over ten years, not a toy for a season."],"id":"soc-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Keeping pets has become increasingly popular, especially among young people living in cities. Analyze the reasons for this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"society","themeName":"社会现象","title":"养宠物热","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"On festival days and in scenic spots, more and more young people can be seen wearing Hanfu, the traditional clothing of the Han people.","note":"场景开头 + 同位语解释 Hanfu 是什么——文化题写专有名词要顺手解释，照顾阅卷人。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What used to appear only in history books and TV dramas has walked into daily life.","note":"what 主语从句 + walked into daily life 拟人，今昔对比一句完成。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Several reasons lie behind the Hanfu fever.","note":"原因段总起句，fever（热潮）点题。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, young people today have a stronger sense of cultural confidence.","note":"cultural confidence（文化自信）是文化主题的头号关键词，必须会写。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"They are proud of traditional Chinese culture and want to express that pride in a visible way.","note":"be proud of、in a visible way（以看得见的方式），把「自信」落到行为上。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, Hanfu is simply beautiful: its flowing sleeves and fine patterns satisfy young people's love of beauty and photography.","note":"冒号后写具体美在哪里：flowing sleeves（飘逸的衣袖）、patterns（纹样），不空喊 beautiful。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Social media spreads this beauty quickly, attracting more followers.","note":"spread 在这里是「传播」，attracting 分词补结果。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Moreover, the growing traditional-culture industry makes Hanfu easier and cheaper to buy than before.","note":"第三条原因落到产业和价格，分析有经济层面，不只谈情怀。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, the Hanfu fever is a welcome sign that traditional culture is coming back to life among the young.","note":"come back to life（复活、重焕生机）点评收束，立意积极。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"As long as the love is sincere, the form it takes matters less.","note":"As long as 条件句收尾：真心比形式重要，评论有分寸。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["On festival days and in scenic spots, more and more young people can be seen wearing Hanfu, the traditional clothing of the Han people. What used to appear only in history books and TV dramas has walked into daily life.","Several reasons lie behind the Hanfu fever. First, young people today have a stronger sense of cultural confidence. They are proud of traditional Chinese culture and want to express that pride in a visible way. Second, Hanfu is simply beautiful: its flowing sleeves and fine patterns satisfy young people's love of beauty and photography. Social media spreads this beauty quickly, attracting more followers. Moreover, the growing traditional-culture industry makes Hanfu easier and cheaper to buy than before.","In my view, the Hanfu fever is a welcome sign that traditional culture is coming back to life among the young. As long as the love is sincere, the form it takes matters less."],"id":"cul-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: In recent years, many young people have fallen in love with Hanfu, traditional Chinese clothing, wearing it for festivals, photos and even daily life. Analyze the reasons for this phenomenon in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"汉服热","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"On weekends, classrooms for calligraphy, painting and tea ceremony are full of children.","note":"场景开头，三个传统技艺名词先把「文化」写具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some people question whether such traditional arts are useful in a modern world of computers.","note":"whether 从句摆出质疑，为表态做靶子。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, learning a traditional art is one of the most worthwhile gifts parents can give a child.","note":"worthwhile（值得的）+ gifts 比喻表态，立场鲜明又有温度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To begin with, traditional arts train qualities that screens cannot.","note":"理由一主题句：与屏幕对比，qualities（品质）一词立住。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Writing calligraphy teaches patience and concentration, since a single careless stroke can ruin a whole work.","note":"stroke（笔画）准词；since 从句用书法的具体规矩论证「练耐心」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Besides, these arts connect children with their own culture in a personal way.","note":"理由二换角度：从个人品质到文化认同。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A child who has ground ink and written Spring Festival couplets understands tradition with his hands, not just from books.","note":"ground ink（研墨）、couplets（春联）文化词地道；with his hands 对比 from books，体验 vs 阅读一句说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The interest may also grow into a lifelong treasure: a hobby that calms the mind, or even a special skill that makes the child stand out in the future.","note":"grow into、stand out（脱颖而出）；冒号展开 lifelong treasure 的两层含义。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, traditional arts are not a burden added to childhood, but a root planted in it.","note":"burden / root 对比收尾：不是负担，是扎根。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"What children learn with their hands today will stay with them for life.","note":"what 主语从句收尾，呼应前文 with his hands，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["On weekends, classrooms for calligraphy, painting and tea ceremony are full of children. Some people question whether such traditional arts are useful in a modern world of computers. In my view, learning a traditional art is one of the most worthwhile gifts parents can give a child.","To begin with, traditional arts train qualities that screens cannot. Writing calligraphy teaches patience and concentration, since a single careless stroke can ruin a whole work. Besides, these arts connect children with their own culture in a personal way. A child who has ground ink and written Spring Festival couplets understands tradition with his hands, not just from books. The interest may also grow into a lifelong treasure: a hobby that calms the mind, or even a special skill that makes the child stand out in the future.","In conclusion, traditional arts are not a burden added to childhood, but a root planted in it. What children learn with their hands today will stay with them for life."],"id":"cul-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some parents send their children to learn traditional arts such as calligraphy, tea ceremony or Chinese painting. Do you think it is worthwhile for children to learn a traditional art? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"要不要从小让孩子学一门传统技艺","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"When Christmas comes, shopping malls fill with trees and lights, and young people exchange gifts and greetings.","note":"场景开头，洋节的热闹先写出来，再引出担忧，文章有起伏。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some people worry that Western festivals are pushing aside our own traditional festivals.","note":"push aside（挤到一边）一句摆出对方担忧，为表态做靶子。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, this worry is unnecessary, as long as we do not forget our own culture.","note":"表态带条件：不必担心，前提是不忘本。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Western festivals spread mainly because they are fun and commercial.","note":"先解释现象成因，观点类也要有分析垫底。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For young people, Christmas is less a religious holiday than a chance to relax, gather with friends and show love to family.","note":"less…than…（与其说是……不如说是……）句式高级，一句点透年轻人过洋节的真实动机。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Enjoying them does not mean giving up our own traditions.","note":"动名词作主语 + does not mean，直接拆掉对方的逻辑。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The Spring Festival still holds an irreplaceable place in Chinese hearts: no festival can match the journey of millions of people traveling home for a family reunion dinner.","note":"irreplaceable（不可替代的）；family reunion dinner（年夜饭/团圆饭）是春节话题必备说法；match 在这里是「比得上」。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"What we should do is not to reject foreign festivals, but to celebrate our own festivals better — making traditional customs lively and attractive to the young again.","note":"What we should do is… 主语从句 + not…but…，对策句：不拒洋节，把自己的节过好。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, cultures grow through exchange.","note":"短句升华收尾：文化因交流而生长。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"An open mind to foreign festivals and a deep love for our own can well exist together.","note":"an open mind / a deep love 对仗收尾，exist together 点出共存立场。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["When Christmas comes, shopping malls fill with trees and lights, and young people exchange gifts and greetings. Some people worry that Western festivals are pushing aside our own traditional festivals. In my view, this worry is unnecessary, as long as we do not forget our own culture.","Western festivals spread mainly because they are fun and commercial. For young people, Christmas is less a religious holiday than a chance to relax, gather with friends and show love to family. Enjoying them does not mean giving up our own traditions. The Spring Festival still holds an irreplaceable place in Chinese hearts: no festival can match the journey of millions of people traveling home for a family reunion dinner. What we should do is not to reject foreign festivals, but to celebrate our own festivals better — making traditional customs lively and attractive to the young again.","In conclusion, cultures grow through exchange. An open mind to foreign festivals and a deep love for our own can well exist together."],"id":"cul-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Western festivals such as Christmas and Valentine's Day are popular among young Chinese people. Some worry this will weaken traditional Chinese festivals. What is your opinion? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"该不该过洋节","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In the past, a museum ticket could cost a family a day's food money.","note":"用「一天的饭钱」量化过去的门票之贵，对比开头有生活气。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Today, most public museums in China open their doors free of charge, and long queues of visitors have become a common sight on weekends.","note":"free of charge（免费）是正式说法，比 free 更书面；common sight 收尾写出现象。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Free admission brings clear benefits.","note":"主题句开启正面段，admission（入场/门票）是本题关键词。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It lowers the door of culture, allowing students, workers and the elderly to enjoy art and history without worrying about the price.","note":"lowers the door（降低门槛）比喻；三类人群并列，好处落到「人人进得来」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Museums thus serve their true purpose of public education, and traditional culture reaches far more people.","note":"thus（从而）承接；serve the purpose of 点出博物馆的本分。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, problems have followed.","note":"最简转折短句开启负面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Huge crowds make visits noisy and rushed, and some visitors behave badly, touching exhibits or leaving rubbish.","note":"两个具体问题并列：拥挤、不文明；exhibits（展品）准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The cost of running museums also falls heavily on the government, since ticket income has disappeared.","note":"fall on（落在……身上）补经济层面的坏处，分析全面。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, free admission is a right policy that should be continued, but it needs better management — such as online booking to control visitor numbers — so that museums stay both open and orderly.","note":"结论带对策：破折号插入具体办法（预约限流），利弊类结尾不止于表态。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In the past, a museum ticket could cost a family a day's food money. Today, most public museums in China open their doors free of charge, and long queues of visitors have become a common sight on weekends.","Free admission brings clear benefits. It lowers the door of culture, allowing students, workers and the elderly to enjoy art and history without worrying about the price. Museums thus serve their true purpose of public education, and traditional culture reaches far more people. However, problems have followed. Huge crowds make visits noisy and rushed, and some visitors behave badly, touching exhibits or leaving rubbish. The cost of running museums also falls heavily on the government, since ticket income has disappeared.","In my view, free admission is a right policy that should be continued, but it needs better management — such as online booking to control visitor numbers — so that museums stay both open and orderly."],"id":"cul-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Most public museums in China are now open to visitors free of charge. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of free admission to museums in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"博物馆免费开放","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In many cities today, children grow up speaking only Mandarin, while the local dialect is heard mainly from grandparents.","note":"while 对比两代人，开头一句写尽方言的处境。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some dialects with few speakers are disappearing quietly, and with them a piece of local culture may be lost forever.","note":"with them 承接：方言消失带走的是文化；lost forever 语气到位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Dialects are worth protecting because they carry far more than sounds.","note":"be worth protecting 先答「是不是问题」，carry far more than sounds 立意高。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"They hold local history, folk stories, jokes and a feeling of home that Mandarin alone cannot fully express.","note":"四个名词并列写方言装着什么；a feeling of home（家乡感）有温度。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When a dialect dies, a community loses part of its memory.","note":"dies 拟人 + memory 比喻，短句点睛。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Protecting dialects does not mean refusing Mandarin, which remains necessary for communication across the country.","note":"先划清边界：保护方言 ≠ 拒绝普通话——观点先站稳，对策才服人。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Practical steps can be taken: families can speak the dialect at home, schools can offer interest courses, and local media can record dialect programs and stories before the oldest speakers are gone.","note":"家庭、学校、媒体三方对策并列；before the oldest speakers are gone 一句点出抢救的紧迫性。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Short-video platforms, interestingly, are already helping, as dialect videos attract millions of young viewers.","note":"interestingly（有意思的是）补一个新现象，对策段有时代感。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In short, Mandarin connects us with the whole country, while dialects connect us with home.","note":"对仗收尾：普通话连国家，方言连家乡——全篇最佳句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A rich culture needs both.","note":"最短句收束，干脆。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["In many cities today, children grow up speaking only Mandarin, while the local dialect is heard mainly from grandparents. Some dialects with few speakers are disappearing quietly, and with them a piece of local culture may be lost forever.","Dialects are worth protecting because they carry far more than sounds. They hold local history, folk stories, jokes and a feeling of home that Mandarin alone cannot fully express. When a dialect dies, a community loses part of its memory. Protecting dialects does not mean refusing Mandarin, which remains necessary for communication across the country. Practical steps can be taken: families can speak the dialect at home, schools can offer interest courses, and local media can record dialect programs and stories before the oldest speakers are gone. Short-video platforms, interestingly, are already helping, as dialect videos attract millions of young viewers.","In short, Mandarin connects us with the whole country, while dialects connect us with home. A rich culture needs both."],"id":"cul-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many local dialects are disappearing as fewer young people can speak them. Is this a problem, and what can be done to protect dialects? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"方言正在消失","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Tom,","note":"书信称呼，格式分先拿。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am so glad that you are interested in the Spring Festival.","note":"回信先回应对方的兴趣，礼貌起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is the most important traditional festival in China, a time when families get together wherever they are.","note":"一句给春节定位；wherever they are（无论身在何处）点出团圆的含义。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The celebration lasts for about two weeks.","note":"主体段先讲时长，总起细节。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Before it arrives, every family cleans the house and prepares plenty of food, hoping for a fresh and lucky start.","note":"hoping for… 分词短语补寓意：扫尘备食为的是新年好开端——介绍习俗要带寓意。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On New Year's Eve, the whole family sits around the table for a big reunion dinner, and dumplings are a must in northern China.","note":"New Year's Eve（除夕）、reunion dinner（团圆饭）、a must（必不可少）都是春节话题的准说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Children receive red packets with lucky money from their elders, and everyone stays up late to welcome the new year.","note":"red packets（红包）、lucky money（压岁钱）文化词译法标准；stay up late 在这里是守岁。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"During the following days, people visit relatives and friends, bringing gifts and good wishes.","note":"时间线推进到拜年，介绍按时间顺序走，条理清楚。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For Chinese people, the Spring Festival is not just a holiday; it is the strongest bond of family love.","note":"not just… 升华：节日是亲情的纽带，bond（纽带）用词准。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I sincerely hope you can come and spend one with my family someday.","note":"结尾发出邀请，介绍信的温度落点；落款 Yours + Li Ming 按题目要求不用真名。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Tom,","I am so glad that you are interested in the Spring Festival. It is the most important traditional festival in China, a time when families get together wherever they are.","The celebration lasts for about two weeks. Before it arrives, every family cleans the house and prepares plenty of food, hoping for a fresh and lucky start. On New Year's Eve, the whole family sits around the table for a big reunion dinner, and dumplings are a must in northern China. Children receive red packets with lucky money from their elders, and everyone stays up late to welcome the new year. During the following days, people visit relatives and friends, bringing gifts and good wishes.","For Chinese people, the Spring Festival is not just a holiday; it is the strongest bond of family love. I sincerely hope you can come and spend one with my family someday.","Yours,","Li Ming"],"id":"cul-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Your foreign friend Tom is interested in the Spring Festival and asks you about it in his letter. Write a reply of 120–180 words introducing the festival. Do not sign your own name; use “Li Ming” instead.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"书信：向外国朋友介绍春节","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"English learning starts early in China, and some parents and teachers worry that it takes time and attention away from Chinese.","note":"一句摆出担忧，take away from（从……夺走）说法准确。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my opinion, learning English well and loving Chinese culture do not conflict with each other; the real problem is imbalance, not English itself.","note":"conflict with（冲突）；分号后一句翻转立意：问题是失衡，不是英语——观点类高分靠这种「找准真问题」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"To begin with, languages are tools for thinking, and a student strong in English reading often becomes better at expressing himself in Chinese as well, because the two support each other.","note":"理由一：语言互通，support each other 点出正向关系。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Many excellent translators are masters of both languages.","note":"短句举例支撑：翻译家双语皆精，一句顶一段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Besides, knowing English opens a window: it allows us to introduce Chinese culture to the world in a language others understand, which protects and spreads our culture better than silence does.","note":"opens a window 比喻；introduce…to the world 是文化输出的准说法；better than silence 对比有力。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Of course, if schools and families praise English scores while ignoring Chinese reading, students will naturally drift away from their own culture.","note":"Of course 让步承认失衡的现实，为对策铺垫。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The solution is balance: solid Chinese education, rich reading in Chinese, and pride in our own traditions.","note":"冒号后三个名词并列给方案；pride in（对……的自豪）收尾。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, English gives us wings, but Chinese gives us roots.","note":"wings / roots 比喻对仗，全篇点睛，值得背。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A student needs both to fly far and stand firm.","note":"fly far / stand firm 与 wings/roots 呼应收尾，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["English learning starts early in China, and some parents and teachers worry that it takes time and attention away from Chinese. In my opinion, learning English well and loving Chinese culture do not conflict with each other; the real problem is imbalance, not English itself.","To begin with, languages are tools for thinking, and a student strong in English reading often becomes better at expressing himself in Chinese as well, because the two support each other. Many excellent translators are masters of both languages. Besides, knowing English opens a window: it allows us to introduce Chinese culture to the world in a language others understand, which protects and spreads our culture better than silence does. Of course, if schools and families praise English scores while ignoring Chinese reading, students will naturally drift away from their own culture. The solution is balance: solid Chinese education, rich reading in Chinese, and pride in our own traditions.","In conclusion, English gives us wings, but Chinese gives us roots. A student needs both to fly far and stand firm."],"id":"cul-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some people worry that spending too much time learning English will weaken students' Chinese and their understanding of Chinese culture. Do you agree? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"学英语会削弱中文吗","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Chinese used to be considered one of the hardest languages in the world, yet today millions of foreigners are learning it with great enthusiasm.","note":"used to be + yet 对比今昔，enthusiasm（热情）点出热度。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"From university classrooms to phone apps, a “Chinese fever” is spreading across the globe.","note":"from…to… 句式扫过场景；spread across the globe 收尾点题。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The strongest reason is China's growing importance in the world.","note":"原因段用最高级排顺序：先讲最强的，层次分明。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"As trade and business with China expand, the ability to speak Chinese has become a valuable skill that brings real job opportunities.","note":"As 引导背景；a valuable skill 点出语言的实用价值，opportunities 落地。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Interest in Chinese culture is another powerful engine.","note":"engine（引擎）比喻引出第二条原因，过渡有新意。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Movies, food, festivals and traditional arts attract foreigners to explore the language behind them.","note":"四个文化名词并列；the language behind them 说法巧妙。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In addition, the Chinese government and universities offer scholarships and exchange programs, making it easier for foreign students to come and learn the language where it is spoken.","note":"scholarships、exchange programs 都是准词；where it is spoken（在语言的母国）收尾点出沉浸式学习。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, the Chinese fever is a natural result of cultural exchange.","note":"评论段先定性：交流的自然结果。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For us Chinese students, it is also a reminder: while the world learns our language, we should know our own culture well enough to introduce it proudly.","note":"评论落到「我们自己」：世界学汉语，我们更要懂自己的文化——立意比单纯自豪高一层。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Chinese used to be considered one of the hardest languages in the world, yet today millions of foreigners are learning it with great enthusiasm. From university classrooms to phone apps, a “Chinese fever” is spreading across the globe.","The strongest reason is China's growing importance in the world. As trade and business with China expand, the ability to speak Chinese has become a valuable skill that brings real job opportunities. Interest in Chinese culture is another powerful engine. Movies, food, festivals and traditional arts attract foreigners to explore the language behind them. In addition, the Chinese government and universities offer scholarships and exchange programs, making it easier for foreign students to come and learn the language where it is spoken.","In my view, the Chinese fever is a natural result of cultural exchange. For us Chinese students, it is also a reminder: while the world learns our language, we should know our own culture well enough to introduce it proudly."],"id":"cul-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: More and more foreigners are learning Chinese, and Chinese language courses are opening in many countries. Analyze the reasons for this “Chinese fever” in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"汉语热","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Walking into many Chinese cities today, one finds old streets rebuilt into bright commercial areas, where ancient-looking buildings house coffee shops and souvenir stores.","note":"分词开头带读者走进现场；where 从句一个画面把现象说清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This way of developing historic areas has brought both praise and criticism.","note":"praise and criticism 预告利弊两面，用词比 advantages/disadvantages 活。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the positive side, rebuilding gives old areas new life.","note":"主题句：重建给老街新生命。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Money from tourism can be used to repair buildings that were falling down, and local people gain jobs and income.","note":"被动句 + 两个好处并列：修楼、就业；fall down（破败倒塌）具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A living street also attracts young visitors who might never enter a quiet museum.","note":"a living street（活过来的街）说法好；对比博物馆点出商业化的独特价值。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"On the negative side, over-commercialization can destroy what makes a place special.","note":"over-commercialization（过度商业化）是本题的核心词，写出来就是分。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When every old street sells the same snacks and goods, its real history and local character disappear, and residents are often pushed out by high rents.","note":"千街一面 + 居民被高房租挤走，两个坏处层层递进；character 在这里是「特色」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, development and protection must go together.","note":"结论先立原则：发展与保护并行。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Old streets should be repaired with respect for their history, keeping their soul while gaining new life — not rebuilt into copies of one another.","note":"soul（灵魂）比喻 + 破折号补刀：不能建成互相复制的街，立意收尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Walking into many Chinese cities today, one finds old streets rebuilt into bright commercial areas, where ancient-looking buildings house coffee shops and souvenir stores. This way of developing historic areas has brought both praise and criticism.","On the positive side, rebuilding gives old areas new life. Money from tourism can be used to repair buildings that were falling down, and local people gain jobs and income. A living street also attracts young visitors who might never enter a quiet museum. On the negative side, over-commercialization can destroy what makes a place special. When every old street sells the same snacks and goods, its real history and local character disappear, and residents are often pushed out by high rents.","In my view, development and protection must go together. Old streets should be repaired with respect for their history, keeping their soul while gaining new life — not rebuilt into copies of one another."],"id":"cul-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many old streets and historic buildings are being rebuilt into modern commercial streets with shops and restaurants. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this practice in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"古街改成商业街","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Peking opera and other traditional operas are treasures of Chinese culture, yet their theatres are filled mostly with grey hair.","note":"grey hair（白发）借代老人，一个细节写尽观众老龄化。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Young people often find opera slow, distant and hard to understand, and this gap threatens the future of the art.","note":"三个形容词并列写年轻人的真实感受；gap（鸿沟）点明问题本质。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Bridging the gap requires changes on both sides.","note":"对策段总起：bridge the gap（弥合鸿沟）与上文呼应。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Opera itself can come closer to the young: shorter performances, clearer stories and modern stage technology can lower the door for first-time audiences.","note":"冒号后三个具体改法并列；lower the door（降低门槛）说法好用。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"New forms are also worth trying — opera elements in popular songs and short videos have already won millions of young fans online.","note":"be worth trying + 破折号举真实例子，对策有时代感。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"At the same time, schools can plant the seed early.","note":"plant the seed（播下种子）比喻引出学校教育这条对策。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"When students sing a few lines, paint facial masks and hear the stories behind famous plays, opera stops being a strange noise and becomes a familiar friend.","note":"三个动词并列写体验课；from noise to friend 对比，效果写活了；facial masks（脸谱）文化词准确。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Young audiences, for their part, only need to give it one real chance before judging.","note":"for their part 把责任分给年轻人一方，对策三方完整；give it one real chance——先体验再评判。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In short, traditional opera does not lack beauty; it lacks a meeting with the young.","note":"does not lack A; it lacks B 对仗收尾：不缺美，缺相遇——点睛句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Building that meeting is our task.","note":"最短句收束，把任务落回「我们」。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Peking opera and other traditional operas are treasures of Chinese culture, yet their theatres are filled mostly with grey hair. Young people often find opera slow, distant and hard to understand, and this gap threatens the future of the art.","Bridging the gap requires changes on both sides. Opera itself can come closer to the young: shorter performances, clearer stories and modern stage technology can lower the door for first-time audiences. New forms are also worth trying — opera elements in popular songs and short videos have already won millions of young fans online. At the same time, schools can plant the seed early. When students sing a few lines, paint facial masks and hear the stories behind famous plays, opera stops being a strange noise and becomes a familiar friend. Young audiences, for their part, only need to give it one real chance before judging.","In short, traditional opera does not lack beauty; it lacks a meeting with the young. Building that meeting is our task."],"id":"cul-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Traditional Chinese operas are losing young audiences, and many young people find them slow and hard to understand. How can traditional opera attract young people again? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"culture","themeName":"文化","title":"年轻人远离传统戏曲","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Early in the morning, long queues form at the library gate.","note":"场景开头一句：清晨图书馆门口的长队，画面先行。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Once inside, many students put books and bags on seats and then disappear for hours, while latecomers wander around looking for an empty chair.","note":"while 对比占座者与找座者，现象的具体不公一句写尽。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Seat-reserving has become a familiar and annoying scene on campus.","note":"seat-reserving（占座）合成词准确；familiar and annoying 定性点题。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The main reason is simple: good seats are limited, especially before exams, while the number of students is large.","note":"原因段一句讲清供需矛盾，冒号展开。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some students reserve seats out of anxiety, fearing they will have nowhere to study; others simply follow what everyone else does.","note":"some…others… 分两类人分析：焦虑的和跟风的，原因有层次。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The harm is clear.","note":"短句切换到危害部分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Reserved but empty seats waste public resources, and quarrels over seats damage the study atmosphere.","note":"两个危害并列：浪费资源 + 破坏氛围；quarrels over（为……争吵）。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A seat is shared property of all students, not a private possession of whoever arrives first with a book.","note":"shared property / private possession 对比立论，whoever 从句收得利落。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my opinion, the problem needs both rules and self-discipline.","note":"评论给出双管齐下的总思路。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Libraries should clear unattended seats after a set time, and students should take only the seat they truly use.","note":"unattended（无人看管的）准词；对策分管理方和学生两方，具体可执行。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A small act of fairness makes the library better for everyone.","note":"fairness（公平）收尾升华，小事见大理。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Early in the morning, long queues form at the library gate. Once inside, many students put books and bags on seats and then disappear for hours, while latecomers wander around looking for an empty chair. Seat-reserving has become a familiar and annoying scene on campus.","The main reason is simple: good seats are limited, especially before exams, while the number of students is large. Some students reserve seats out of anxiety, fearing they will have nowhere to study; others simply follow what everyone else does. The harm is clear. Reserved but empty seats waste public resources, and quarrels over seats damage the study atmosphere. A seat is shared property of all students, not a private possession of whoever arrives first with a book.","In my opinion, the problem needs both rules and self-discipline. Libraries should clear unattended seats after a set time, and students should take only the seat they truly use. A small act of fairness makes the library better for everyone."],"id":"cam-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: In many university libraries, students leave books and bags on seats early in the morning to reserve them, while others cannot find a place to study. Analyze this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"图书馆占座","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Wang Lei,","note":"道歉信称呼，对象是题目给定的同学。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing to say how sorry I am for missing our appointment last Saturday.","note":"第一句直奔道歉：miss an appointment（爽约）是本题核心说法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I know you waited for me at the library gate for nearly an hour, and I completely understand why you are upset.","note":"先承认对方的损失和情绪再解释——道歉信的顺序就是分寸。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Something urgent happened in my family that morning, and I had to rush home at once.","note":"简要交代原因，urgent、at once 用词利落；原因只写一句，不喧宾夺主。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In the hurry, my phone ran out of battery, so I could not call or message you — but that is an explanation, not an excuse.","note":"an explanation, not an excuse（是说明，不是借口）一句显诚意，道歉信的点睛句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I should have found a way to let you know, and I truly regret wasting your time and breaking my word.","note":"should have done（本该做却没做）表自责；break one's word（失信）准词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Our group project still needs the discussion we planned.","note":"转到补救：先点出未完成的正事。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Could we meet this Wednesday evening instead?","note":"Could we…? 礼貌提出新的具体时间，补救要落到日期。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I will bring the materials I have prepared, and dinner afterwards is on me as a small apology.","note":"is on me（我请客）地道说法；补救有诚意有行动。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Please forgive me this time.","note":"结尾请求原谅，道歉信收束的礼节。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I promise it will never happen again.","note":"补一句保证，落款 Yours sincerely + Li Ming 按要求不用真名——格式完整。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Wang Lei,","I am writing to say how sorry I am for missing our appointment last Saturday. I know you waited for me at the library gate for nearly an hour, and I completely understand why you are upset.","Something urgent happened in my family that morning, and I had to rush home at once. In the hurry, my phone ran out of battery, so I could not call or message you — but that is an explanation, not an excuse. I should have found a way to let you know, and I truly regret wasting your time and breaking my word. Our group project still needs the discussion we planned. Could we meet this Wednesday evening instead? I will bring the materials I have prepared, and dinner afterwards is on me as a small apology.","Please forgive me this time. I promise it will never happen again.","Yours sincerely,","Li Ming"],"id":"cam-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: You failed to keep an appointment with your classmate Wang Lei last weekend because of a sudden family matter, and he was upset. Write a letter of apology of 120–180 words to him. Do not sign your own name; use “Li Ming” instead.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"道歉信：爽约","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In the first weeks of the term, club recruitment fills the campus with posters and tents.","note":"场景开头：海报和帐篷，招新季的画面立现；recruitment（招新）准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"For a freshman, joining clubs is a tempting but confusing choice.","note":"tempting but confusing（诱人又纠结）一句写出新生的真实心态。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, freshmen should join one or two clubs that truly interest them — but no more.","note":"表态带数量限定，破折号补一句 but no more，立场具体可操作。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Clubs offer things classrooms cannot.","note":"理由段主题句：社团给的是课堂给不了的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In a photography club or a debate team, students make friends across majors, practice real skills and learn to organize activities, all of which build confidence and teamwork.","note":"两个具体社团 + 三个动词并列 + all of which 收束，好处写得扎实。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Club life also gives freshmen a sense of belonging in a strange new place.","note":"a sense of belonging（归属感）是校园话题的核心词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, joining too many clubs is a trap.","note":"trap（陷阱）比喻转折，开启反面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Meetings and activities eat up evenings and weekends, leaving students exhausted and their studies behind.","note":"eat up（耗尽）形象；leaving… 分词补结果。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some freshmen join clubs only to follow roommates, and quit within weeks, having wasted both time and fees.","note":"点出跟风入团的具体后果，having wasted 分词收尾紧凑。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In conclusion, clubs are a valuable part of university life when chosen with care.","note":"结论带条件：用心选才有价值。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Quality matters far more than quantity: one club loved deeply beats five joined blindly.","note":"quality / quantity 对比 + 冒号举例收尾：一深胜五滥，值得背。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In the first weeks of the term, club recruitment fills the campus with posters and tents. For a freshman, joining clubs is a tempting but confusing choice. In my view, freshmen should join one or two clubs that truly interest them — but no more.","Clubs offer things classrooms cannot. In a photography club or a debate team, students make friends across majors, practice real skills and learn to organize activities, all of which build confidence and teamwork. Club life also gives freshmen a sense of belonging in a strange new place. However, joining too many clubs is a trap. Meetings and activities eat up evenings and weekends, leaving students exhausted and their studies behind. Some freshmen join clubs only to follow roommates, and quit within weeks, having wasted both time and fees.","In conclusion, clubs are a valuable part of university life when chosen with care. Quality matters far more than quantity: one club loved deeply beats five joined blindly."],"id":"cam-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: When freshmen arrive on campus, many clubs try to recruit them. Some students join several clubs, while others join none. Do you think freshmen should join student clubs? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大一要不要加入社团","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"For most students, the dormitory is the first place where they live closely with strangers.","note":"一句点出宿舍生活的本质：第一次与陌生人密切共处，问题由此而来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Different living habits soon bring small conflicts: one roommate plays games late into the night, another never cleans, and a third turns on the light at dawn.","note":"冒号后 one…another…a third… 三个室友三个毛病，画面感拉满。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Such problems are usually not caused by bad people, but by different routines and a lack of communication.","note":"not…but… 找准根源：不是人坏，是习惯不同 + 不沟通——分析有洞察。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Many students suffer in silence until anger bursts out, which makes a small matter much worse.","note":"suffer in silence（默默忍受）、burst out（爆发）把矛盾升级的过程写活。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The way out is to talk early and set rules together.","note":"对策段主题句：早沟通、立规矩。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Roommates can agree on quiet hours after eleven, take turns cleaning, and respect each other's need for personal space.","note":"三条规矩并列，全是可执行的；take turns（轮流）、personal space 都是准说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"When a problem appears, speaking honestly and kindly is far better than complaining behind someone's back.","note":"behind someone's back（背后抱怨）地道；对比出正确做法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"After all, small compromises are the price of living together, and they are also lessons in getting along with society.","note":"After all 升华：妥协是共处的价格，也是走向社会的课。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, a harmonious dormitory is not found but built — by respect, communication and a willingness to give way a little.","note":"not found but built 对仗收尾；give way（让步）点睛。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["For most students, the dormitory is the first place where they live closely with strangers. Different living habits soon bring small conflicts: one roommate plays games late into the night, another never cleans, and a third turns on the light at dawn.","Such problems are usually not caused by bad people, but by different routines and a lack of communication. Many students suffer in silence until anger bursts out, which makes a small matter much worse. The way out is to talk early and set rules together. Roommates can agree on quiet hours after eleven, take turns cleaning, and respect each other's need for personal space. When a problem appears, speaking honestly and kindly is far better than complaining behind someone's back. After all, small compromises are the price of living together, and they are also lessons in getting along with society.","In short, a harmonious dormitory is not found but built — by respect, communication and a willingness to give way a little."],"id":"cam-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Living with roommates is not always easy. Different habits often cause conflicts in dormitories. What are the common problems, and how can roommates get along better? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"室友矛盾怎么解","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"On many campuses today, students run with their phones in hand, checking in at fixed points to complete the running distance required by their PE course.","note":"场景开头把「跑步打卡」写给不熟悉的读者看，check in（打卡）准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This rule has won both support and complaints.","note":"一句预告利弊两方，won support and complaints 说法简练。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Supporters point out that the rule works.","note":"Supporters point out… 引用一方的句式，利弊类好用。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many students who would never exercise on their own are pushed outdoors, and after a term of regular running, their health and energy clearly improve.","note":"on their own（主动地）；用结果（健康改善）论证规则有效。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The requirement also helps students form an exercise habit, which may benefit them for years.","note":"form a habit（养成习惯）；好处落到长远。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, complaints are not groundless.","note":"not groundless（不是没道理）转折，开启反面，语气客观。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Some students cheat by riding bicycles slowly or asking friends to carry their phones, which makes the rule meaningless.","note":"两个作弊细节真实又好笑，批评有据；cheat 用词直接。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Others feel that forced exercise kills their interest in sports, turning something joyful into a boring task to finish.","note":"kill interest（扼杀兴趣）+ turn…into…，第二层坏处落到心理层面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, the purpose of the rule is good, but its form should be more flexible.","note":"结论分目的与形式两层看，不简单站队。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Offering choices — running, swimming, ball games — would keep the goal of health while respecting students' different interests.","note":"破折号列出选项给具体改法；respect interests 收尾，方案完整。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["On many campuses today, students run with their phones in hand, checking in at fixed points to complete the running distance required by their PE course. This rule has won both support and complaints.","Supporters point out that the rule works. Many students who would never exercise on their own are pushed outdoors, and after a term of regular running, their health and energy clearly improve. The requirement also helps students form an exercise habit, which may benefit them for years. However, complaints are not groundless. Some students cheat by riding bicycles slowly or asking friends to carry their phones, which makes the rule meaningless. Others feel that forced exercise kills their interest in sports, turning something joyful into a boring task to finish.","In my view, the purpose of the rule is good, but its form should be more flexible. Offering choices — running, swimming, ball games — would keep the goal of health while respecting students' different interests."],"id":"cam-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many universities require students to complete a certain number of running check-ins each term for their PE grade. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of this requirement in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"校园跑打卡该不该强制","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"NOTICE","note":"通知格式第一项：标题 NOTICE 居中，格式分先拿。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To provide students with a stage to show their English ability and build their confidence, the English Club will hold an English speech contest with the theme “My University, My Dream” on Friday, December 18, in Lecture Hall 2 of the Teaching Building.","note":"通知的第一句要把五要素说全：目的、主办方、活动、主题、时间、地点——一句不缺。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The contest is open to all students of the university.","note":"交代参加对象，通知的必备信息。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Each speech should be about three minutes long and closely related to the theme.","note":"交代具体要求，closely related to（紧扣）准说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Participants are asked to sign up at the office of the English Club or through the club's WeChat account before December 10.","note":"sign up（报名）是活动通知的核心词；报名方式和截止时间都要写。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Speeches will be judged on content, language and delivery, and the top ten speakers will receive certificates and prizes.","note":"被动句交代评奖标准和奖励，judge on（依据……评判）地道。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A training session on speech skills will also be offered to all participants on December 13.","note":"补一条附加安排，通知信息更完整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"This is a valuable chance to challenge yourself and make your voice heard.","note":"结尾动员句：make your voice heard（让你的声音被听到）说法出彩。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"We warmly welcome students from all majors to take part.","note":"落款 The English Club + 日期 December 1——通知落款要有单位和日期，缺一扣分。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["NOTICE","To provide students with a stage to show their English ability and build their confidence, the English Club will hold an English speech contest with the theme “My University, My Dream” on Friday, December 18, in Lecture Hall 2 of the Teaching Building.","The contest is open to all students of the university. Each speech should be about three minutes long and closely related to the theme. Participants are asked to sign up at the office of the English Club or through the club's WeChat account before December 10. Speeches will be judged on content, language and delivery, and the top ten speakers will receive certificates and prizes. A training session on speech skills will also be offered to all participants on December 13.","This is a valuable chance to challenge yourself and make your voice heard. We warmly welcome students from all majors to take part.","The English Club","December 1"],"id":"cam-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: The English Club of your university is going to hold an English speech contest. Write a notice of 120–180 words to inform students of the contest and call for participants.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"通知：英语演讲比赛","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Every term, course selection starts a familiar debate: should one choose easy courses that promise high marks, or difficult courses that promise real gains?","note":"冒号引出争议问题，high marks / real gains 对仗，题目一句摆清。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, a wise student aims mainly at useful courses, using easy ones only as a small balance.","note":"表态带分寸：以有用为主、水课只作调剂，aim at（以……为目标）。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Marks matter, but they are not the purpose of university.","note":"短句让步后立论，节奏干脆。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"An easy course may add a few points to one's average, yet leave the mind empty after the exam.","note":"add points ↔ leave the mind empty 对比，水课的代价一句写透。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A challenging course, by contrast, forces students to read widely, think deeply and solve real problems; the abilities gained stay useful long after the marks are forgotten.","note":"by contrast 切换；三个动词并列；long after 时间对比收尾，难课的价值立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Admittedly, a term filled only with the hardest courses may bring heavy pressure and even hurt one's confidence.","note":"Admittedly 让步，承认全选难课的风险。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"That is why balance is needed.","note":"That is why… 短句承接，推出「平衡」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"But balance should serve learning, not replace it.","note":"serve / replace 对比，把让步拉回立场，观点不被稀释。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, we come to university to grow, not merely to collect high marks.","note":"not merely（不只是）收尾重申目的。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Choose the courses that make you better, and let the marks follow.","note":"祈使句结尾：选让你变好的课，分数自会跟上——好背的金句。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Every term, course selection starts a familiar debate: should one choose easy courses that promise high marks, or difficult courses that promise real gains? In my view, a wise student aims mainly at useful courses, using easy ones only as a small balance.","Marks matter, but they are not the purpose of university. An easy course may add a few points to one's average, yet leave the mind empty after the exam. A challenging course, by contrast, forces students to read widely, think deeply and solve real problems; the abilities gained stay useful long after the marks are forgotten. Admittedly, a term filled only with the hardest courses may bring heavy pressure and even hurt one's confidence. That is why balance is needed. But balance should serve learning, not replace it.","In conclusion, we come to university to grow, not merely to collect high marks. Choose the courses that make you better, and let the marks follow."],"id":"cam-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: When choosing elective courses, some students pick easy courses with high marks, while others choose difficult but useful ones. Which do you think is a wiser choice? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"该不该选水课","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Every June, the roads near the dormitories turn into busy markets.","note":"时间 + 地点开头，turn into 点出现象变化。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Graduating students spread out their books, bicycles, lamps and even quilts on the ground, and younger students crowd around hunting for bargains.","note":"四个货物名词 + hunt for bargains（淘便宜货），市场画面全出来了。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The graduation market has become a special scene of campus life.","note":"短句点题收束首段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Its popularity is easy to understand.","note":"原因段总起句，过渡自然。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"For graduates, things they cannot take away would otherwise be thrown away; selling them at low prices turns waste into money and memories into gifts.","note":"For graduates / For buyers 对称分析两方；turns waste into money and memories into gifts 对仗，是全篇最亮的一句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"For buyers, the prices are friendly and the goods are exactly what campus life needs — a senior's used textbook with careful notes may be worth more than a new one.","note":"破折号举例：带笔记的旧教材比新书值钱——细节有校园味。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Behind the trade is also a green idea: passing useful things to new hands instead of wasting them.","note":"倒装句 Behind the trade is… 引出第三层原因：环保理念。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, the graduation market is more than a market.","note":"评论句先立意：不只是市场。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"It is a small ceremony of passing on, where seniors leave not only their goods but also their stories to those who follow.","note":"ceremony（仪式）比喻 + not only…but also… 收尾：留下的是物品也是故事，温情落点。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Every June, the roads near the dormitories turn into busy markets. Graduating students spread out their books, bicycles, lamps and even quilts on the ground, and younger students crowd around hunting for bargains. The graduation market has become a special scene of campus life.","Its popularity is easy to understand. For graduates, things they cannot take away would otherwise be thrown away; selling them at low prices turns waste into money and memories into gifts. For buyers, the prices are friendly and the goods are exactly what campus life needs — a senior's used textbook with careful notes may be worth more than a new one. Behind the trade is also a green idea: passing useful things to new hands instead of wasting them.","In my view, the graduation market is more than a market. It is a small ceremony of passing on, where seniors leave not only their goods but also their stories to those who follow."],"id":"cam-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: At the end of every term, graduating students sell their books, bicycles and daily goods on campus at low prices, and these graduation markets are always crowded. Analyze this phenomenon in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"校园二手市场火爆","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"At half past eleven, the battle begins.","note":"battle 比喻开头，食堂抢饭的紧张感一句立住。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Hundreds of students rush to the canteen at the same time, queues stretch to the door, and finding a seat becomes a matter of luck.","note":"三个短句并列推进画面；a matter of luck（全靠运气）说法鲜活。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The lunch-time crowd is a daily headache for both students and canteen staff.","note":"a daily headache（每天的头疼事）比喻点题。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The root of the problem is that everyone eats at the same time and in the same few places.","note":"The root of the problem is that… 找根源：不是人多，是同时同地——对策由此推出。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Solving it therefore requires spreading people out in time and space.","note":"therefore 承接根源给出总思路：时间和空间上分流，逻辑链漂亮。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, the university can arrange class hours more flexibly, so that not all students finish class at exactly the same moment.","note":"对策一从源头错峰：flexibly（灵活地）；so that 目的从句。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Second, canteens can open more windows at peak hours and offer takeaway and pre-order services, allowing students to pick up food quickly without queuing.","note":"at peak hours（高峰时段）、pre-order（预订）都是准词；对策具体到窗口和服务。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Students themselves can also help by avoiding the busiest half hour when their schedule allows, and by leaving seats promptly after eating instead of chatting over empty trays.","note":"第三条落到学生自己：错峰 + 吃完就走；over empty trays（对着空盘子聊天）细节真实。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, the crowd is not caused by too many students, but by too many students at the same time.","note":"not…but… 收尾重申根源，与主体段首尾呼应。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Spread them out, and the problem is half solved.","note":"祈使句 + half solved，结尾干脆好记。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["At half past eleven, the battle begins. Hundreds of students rush to the canteen at the same time, queues stretch to the door, and finding a seat becomes a matter of luck. The lunch-time crowd is a daily headache for both students and canteen staff.","The root of the problem is that everyone eats at the same time and in the same few places. Solving it therefore requires spreading people out in time and space. First, the university can arrange class hours more flexibly, so that not all students finish class at exactly the same moment. Second, canteens can open more windows at peak hours and offer takeaway and pre-order services, allowing students to pick up food quickly without queuing. Students themselves can also help by avoiding the busiest half hour when their schedule allows, and by leaving seats promptly after eating instead of chatting over empty trays.","In short, the crowd is not caused by too many students, but by too many students at the same time. Spread them out, and the problem is half solved."],"id":"cam-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: At lunch time, university canteens are always overcrowded, with long queues and no empty seats. How can this problem be eased? Write 120–180 words with your suggestions.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"食堂排队与占座","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Part-time jobs are common on campus: tutoring, delivering food, working in coffee shops.","note":"冒号后三个具体兼职，现象不用抽象讲。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some teachers worry that earning money will steal students' study time.","note":"摆出担忧，steal time（偷走时间）说法形象。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, a suitable part-time job is good for students, provided it never becomes more important than study.","note":"表态带 provided（只要）条件从句，立场有边界。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A part-time job teaches what textbooks cannot.","note":"理由段主题句：兼职教的是课本教不了的。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"By earning money themselves, students learn the value of money and become more independent of their families.","note":"By… 分词式开头；the value of money、independent of 都是准搭配。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Working also gives them early experience of society: how to communicate with strangers, manage time and solve real problems.","note":"冒号后三个 how to 并列，社会经验写具体。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"These abilities will help greatly when they look for real jobs.","note":"短句承接：能力落到将来求职。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Of course, a job that takes too many hours is a different story.","note":"a different story（那就是另一回事了）让步转折，地道口语化书面语。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If a student returns to the dormitory exhausted every night and sleeps through morning classes, the job is costing far more than it pays.","note":"if 条件句算账：costing more than it pays（付出大于收入），让步段的点睛句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, part-time jobs are a valuable lesson outside the classroom.","note":"a lesson outside the classroom 定位收尾。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The rule is simple: study first, work second, and choose jobs that leave you stronger, not weaker.","note":"冒号 + 对仗短句给出原则，stronger / weaker 对比好记。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Part-time jobs are common on campus: tutoring, delivering food, working in coffee shops. Some teachers worry that earning money will steal students' study time. In my view, a suitable part-time job is good for students, provided it never becomes more important than study.","A part-time job teaches what textbooks cannot. By earning money themselves, students learn the value of money and become more independent of their families. Working also gives them early experience of society: how to communicate with strangers, manage time and solve real problems. These abilities will help greatly when they look for real jobs. Of course, a job that takes too many hours is a different story. If a student returns to the dormitory exhausted every night and sleeps through morning classes, the job is costing far more than it pays.","In conclusion, part-time jobs are a valuable lesson outside the classroom. The rule is simple: study first, work second, and choose jobs that leave you stronger, not weaker."],"id":"cam-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many college students take part-time jobs, but some teachers worry that jobs will affect their studies. Do you think college students should take part-time jobs? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"campus","themeName":"校园生活","title":"大学生要不要做兼职","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Standing at the crossroads of graduation, every student faces the same question: work now, or study further?","note":"crossroads（十字路口）比喻 + 冒号引出问题，职业规划题的经典开场。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"There is no standard answer, but in my view, the choice should be based on one's major, ability and long-term goal rather than on what most classmates are doing.","note":"先承认无标准答案再给判断标准，三个依据并列；rather than 点出「不跟风」。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Further study suits those whose fields require deep knowledge, such as medicine and research, and it often opens doors to better positions in the future.","note":"pursue further study 的同义说法；open doors（打开机会之门）比喻好用。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Direct employment, on the other hand, allows students to gain real experience early and become financially independent sooner; in fast-changing industries, three years of practice may teach more than three years in a classroom.","note":"on the other hand 对称开启另一方；分号后用「三年 vs 三年」对比，论证有分量。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The worst choice is the blind one — taking the postgraduate exam only to escape the pressure of job hunting, or rushing into work without any plan.","note":"破折号展开「最差的选择」：为逃避而考研、没计划就就业，两头都点到。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, both roads can lead to a bright future.","note":"短句收束：两条路都能通向好未来。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The key is to choose the one that fits your own direction, and then walk it with full effort.","note":"fits your own direction（适合自己的方向）收尾，建议落点清楚。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Standing at the crossroads of graduation, every student faces the same question: work now, or study further? There is no standard answer, but in my view, the choice should be based on one's major, ability and long-term goal rather than on what most classmates are doing.","Further study suits those whose fields require deep knowledge, such as medicine and research, and it often opens doors to better positions in the future. Direct employment, on the other hand, allows students to gain real experience early and become financially independent sooner; in fast-changing industries, three years of practice may teach more than three years in a classroom. The worst choice is the blind one — taking the postgraduate exam only to escape the pressure of job hunting, or rushing into work without any plan.","In conclusion, both roads can lead to a bright future. The key is to choose the one that fits your own direction, and then walk it with full effort."],"id":"car-m1","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Upon graduation, some students look for a job directly, while others choose to pursue postgraduate study. Which choice do you think is better? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业后先就业还是先考研","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"“What should I do after graduation?” is a question that troubles many college students.","note":"直接引用内心的问句开头，代入感强，问题解决型好起手。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Some change their minds every month, while others simply follow the crowd.","note":"follow the crowd（随大流）一句点出第二种迷茫的样子。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Behind this confusion lie both personal and social reasons.","note":"倒装句 Behind…lie… 开启原因段，句式有变化。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Many students know little about real jobs because their life has been limited to classrooms and exams; without experience, every career looks equally strange.","note":"分号因果：没经验，所以哪个职业都陌生——根源找得准。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"At the same time, too many choices and too much advice from family and the Internet make the decision even harder.","note":"too many / too much 并列第二个原因：选择和声音太多。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"To find a direction, students should start with action rather than pure thinking.","note":"对策段总思路：先行动，别空想——立意关键。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Trying internships, part-time jobs and club work in different fields quickly shows what they enjoy and what they are good at.","note":"三个尝试并列 + 两个 what 从句：喜欢什么、擅长什么，方向就从这两点来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Talking to senior students and professionals also turns an unknown future into real, touchable examples.","note":"touchable（摸得着的）说法形象；turn…into… 句型复现。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"A career direction is rarely found in one day; it is built step by step through small experiences.","note":"分号对仗：方向不是找到的，是攒出来的——全篇立意句。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, confusion is normal at twenty, but it should push us to explore, not to wait.","note":"收尾先安慰再推动：迷茫正常，但要探索不要等。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The road appears only when we start walking.","note":"最短句收尾：路是走出来的，金句式结尾。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["“What should I do after graduation?” is a question that troubles many college students. Some change their minds every month, while others simply follow the crowd. Behind this confusion lie both personal and social reasons.","Many students know little about real jobs because their life has been limited to classrooms and exams; without experience, every career looks equally strange. At the same time, too many choices and too much advice from family and the Internet make the decision even harder. To find a direction, students should start with action rather than pure thinking. Trying internships, part-time jobs and club work in different fields quickly shows what they enjoy and what they are good at. Talking to senior students and professionals also turns an unknown future into real, touchable examples. A career direction is rarely found in one day; it is built step by step through small experiences.","In short, confusion is normal at twenty, but it should push us to explore, not to wait. The road appears only when we start walking."],"id":"car-m10","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many college students feel confused about their future career and have no clear plan. What causes this confusion, and what can students do to find their direction? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"对未来职业没有方向","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"In recent years, a new word has appeared in discussions about graduates: “slow employment”.","note":"冒号引出新概念，现象类开头先给新词下定义域。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Instead of rushing into the job market, some young people take months or even a year to travel, study or simply think about what they really want.","note":"instead of 对比旧做法；what they really want 点出慢就业的积极面。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Several reasons explain this choice.","note":"原因段总起句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, many graduates are not clear about their direction; a pause helps them avoid starting a job they will hate and quit soon.","note":"分号因果：方向不清 → 先停一停，避免入错行又辞职。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In addition, families today are generally better off, so parents can support a short break that was impossible in the past.","note":"better off（经济更宽裕）准词组；补经济层面的原因。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, slow employment has a risky side.","note":"转折短句开启风险面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A long gap with no plan can turn rest into idleness, and employers may question what a graduate did during empty months.","note":"turn rest into idleness（把休息变闲散）对比精准；empty months 说法形象。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Time itself is also a cost that cannot be earned back.","note":"短句点出最根本的代价：时间成本不可逆。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, a short, planned pause is reasonable and can even be valuable.","note":"评论带两个限定词：short、planned——分寸感就是分。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"But slow employment should be a bridge to a clearer future, not an escape from reality.","note":"bridge / escape 对比收尾，与前文呼应，立意稳。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["In recent years, a new word has appeared in discussions about graduates: “slow employment”. Instead of rushing into the job market, some young people take months or even a year to travel, study or simply think about what they really want.","Several reasons explain this choice. To begin with, many graduates are not clear about their direction; a pause helps them avoid starting a job they will hate and quit soon. In addition, families today are generally better off, so parents can support a short break that was impossible in the past. However, slow employment has a risky side. A long gap with no plan can turn rest into idleness, and employers may question what a graduate did during empty months. Time itself is also a cost that cannot be earned back.","In my view, a short, planned pause is reasonable and can even be valuable. But slow employment should be a bridge to a clearer future, not an escape from reality."],"id":"car-m2","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some graduates are in no hurry to find a job after graduation, choosing instead to travel, prepare for further study or rest for a while. This is known as “slow employment”. Analyze this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"慢就业","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Starting a business has become a dream for many young graduates.","note":"动名词作主语开篇，start a business（创业）是本题核心说法。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"With a good idea and a small team, some hope to build their own company rather than send out resumes.","note":"send out resumes（投简历）细节真实；rather than 对比两种选择。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"This choice is exciting, but it is also full of risks.","note":"一句预告利弊：exciting / risks 两面都点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, running one's own business offers freedom and fast growth.","note":"主题句开启正面段。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Young founders can follow their own ideas, make decisions quickly and learn in one year what a normal job might teach in five.","note":"founders（创始人）准词；one year vs five 对比量化「成长快」。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Success, when it comes, brings both income and a strong sense of achievement.","note":"a sense of achievement（成就感）是职业话题高频词组。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On the other hand, the failure rate is high.","note":"failure rate（失败率）转折开启负面段，一词定调。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Most new businesses die within three years because of limited money, little experience and fierce competition.","note":"die 拟人；三个原因并列：钱、经验、竞争——创业失败的经典三因。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Graduates also lack the connections and management skills that business requires, and failure may leave them with debts and lost years.","note":"connections（人脉）、management skills（管理能力）都是创业话题的准词；debts（债务）、lost years 把失败代价写具体。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"In my view, starting a business is admirable, but graduates should prepare carefully first — perhaps by working in the industry for a while — instead of jumping in with nothing but passion.","note":"结论带对策：先入行积累再创业；nothing but passion（只有热情）一句点醒冲动创业。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Starting a business has become a dream for many young graduates. With a good idea and a small team, some hope to build their own company rather than send out resumes. This choice is exciting, but it is also full of risks.","On the one hand, running one's own business offers freedom and fast growth. Young founders can follow their own ideas, make decisions quickly and learn in one year what a normal job might teach in five. Success, when it comes, brings both income and a strong sense of achievement. On the other hand, the failure rate is high. Most new businesses die within three years because of limited money, little experience and fierce competition. Graduates also lack the connections and management skills that business requires, and failure may leave them with debts and lost years.","In my view, starting a business is admirable, but graduates should prepare carefully first — perhaps by working in the industry for a while — instead of jumping in with nothing but passion."],"id":"car-m3","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Some graduates choose to start their own business instead of working for others. Discuss the advantages and disadvantages of starting a business right after graduation in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"毕业后自己创业","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Sending out resume after resume and hearing nothing back is a painful experience shared by many graduates.","note":"resume after resume（简历一份接一份）排比式开头，求职之难一秒共情。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"After weeks of silence and failed interviews, some begin to doubt their own ability.","note":"doubt one's ability 点出心理后果，问题不只是没工作。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The situation is hard, but it is not hopeless.","note":"短句定调：难，但有解——问题解决型的信心句。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"First, it helps to find the real reasons.","note":"对策段先诊断后开方，顺序专业。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A resume that lists courses but no skills or experience gives employers little reason to call.","note":"一针见血指出简历的通病：只有课程、没有能力证据。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Applying for every position without a clear target also wastes energy, since each job requires different strengths.","note":"动名词作主语指出第二个原因：海投无目标；since 从句讲清道理。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"With the reasons clear, action can be taken.","note":"With 短语过渡到具体行动，段落衔接漂亮。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Graduates should rebuild their resumes around what employers want: skills, internships and projects placed first.","note":"冒号列出简历该放前面的三样：技能、实习、项目——实用建议。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"They should also widen their choices — smaller companies and new industries often offer chances that famous companies do not.","note":"破折号补具体方向：小公司和新行业，对策拓宽思路。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Most importantly, every failed interview should be reviewed as a lesson, not remembered as a shame.","note":"as a lesson, not as a shame 对比，心态层面的建议压轴。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In short, job hunting is a process of matching and improving.","note":"matching（匹配）一词点出求职本质，收尾立意。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Those who keep learning from failure will finally meet the job that fits them.","note":"Those who… 收尾展望，fits them 与全文呼应。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Sending out resume after resume and hearing nothing back is a painful experience shared by many graduates. After weeks of silence and failed interviews, some begin to doubt their own ability. The situation is hard, but it is not hopeless.","First, it helps to find the real reasons. A resume that lists courses but no skills or experience gives employers little reason to call. Applying for every position without a clear target also wastes energy, since each job requires different strengths. With the reasons clear, action can be taken. Graduates should rebuild their resumes around what employers want: skills, internships and projects placed first. They should also widen their choices — smaller companies and new industries often offer chances that famous companies do not. Most importantly, every failed interview should be reviewed as a lesson, not remembered as a shame.","In short, job hunting is a process of matching and improving. Those who keep learning from failure will finally meet the job that fits them."],"id":"car-m4","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many graduates send out dozens of resumes but receive few replies, and some lose confidence after repeated failures in job hunting. What are the possible reasons, and what should they do? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"求职屡屡碰壁","type":"问题解决型","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Dear Sir or Madam,","note":"求职信称呼：不知道姓名时用 Dear Sir or Madam，格式要点。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am writing to apply for the summer internship position in software development advertised on your company's website.","note":"第一句三要素：目的（apply for）、岗位、信息来源——求职信开头必须一句说全。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"I am a junior student majoring in computer science, and I believe my skills and experience make me a suitable candidate for this position.","note":"major in（主修）、candidate（候选人）都是求职信准词；junior 是大三，别写成 grade three。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"During the past three years, I have built a solid foundation in programming, with good command of C and Python, and I have completed two course projects in a team, one of which won a university-level prize.","note":"主体段用事实说话：基础、语言、项目、获奖；a good command of（熟练掌握）是简历高频说法。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Last summer, I worked as a volunteer in our school's IT service center, helping students and teachers solve computer problems, which trained my communication skills and patience.","note":"一段相关经历 + which 从句点出练到的能力——经历要落到能力上。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"I am a quick learner, careful with details, and always willing to take responsibility.","note":"三个自我评价并列：学得快、细心、肯担当，都是雇主爱听的词。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"I would be grateful if you could give me an opportunity for an interview.","note":"结尾请求面试的礼貌句式：I would be grateful if…，求职信必备。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"My resume is attached for your consideration.","note":"attached（附上）、for your consideration（供您考虑）是附件说明的固定说法。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Thank you for your time, and I look forward to hearing from you.","note":"致谢 + 期待回复，落款 Yours faithfully（不知姓名时用 faithfully，知道姓名用 sincerely）+ Li Ming 按要求不用真名。","tag":"好结构"}],"essay":["Dear Sir or Madam,","I am writing to apply for the summer internship position in software development advertised on your company's website. I am a junior student majoring in computer science, and I believe my skills and experience make me a suitable candidate for this position.","During the past three years, I have built a solid foundation in programming, with good command of C and Python, and I have completed two course projects in a team, one of which won a university-level prize. Last summer, I worked as a volunteer in our school's IT service center, helping students and teachers solve computer problems, which trained my communication skills and patience. I am a quick learner, careful with details, and always willing to take responsibility.","I would be grateful if you could give me an opportunity for an interview. My resume is attached for your consideration. Thank you for your time, and I look forward to hearing from you.","Yours faithfully,","Li Ming"],"id":"car-m5","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: You are a junior student of computer science. Write a letter of application of 120–180 words to a software company, applying for a summer internship position. Do not sign your own name; use “Li Ming” instead.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"求职信：应聘实习岗位","type":"应用文","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"A high-paying job you dislike, or a loved job with a modest salary?","note":"名词短语 + 问句开场，把选择的两难一句摆出，观点类好钩子。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"This is the first hard choice many graduates must make.","note":"短句承接，点明话题分量。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"In my view, interest should come first for a first job, though salary can never be completely ignored.","note":"表态带 though 让步：兴趣优先，但薪水不能无视——分寸感。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A career lasts for decades, and interest is what keeps a person growing through those years.","note":"what 主语从句（强调句式）：用「几十年」的尺度论证兴趣，格局打开。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Someone who loves his work learns faster, works more willingly and is more likely to become truly good at it — and income usually follows ability in the end.","note":"三个动词并列推演因果链，最后 income follows ability 一句反打薪水派。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Salary, by contrast, can be a trap.","note":"by contrast 转折，trap 比喻开启反面。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A boring but well-paid job slowly eats away a young person's energy and curiosity, and after a few years, changing direction becomes costly.","note":"eat away（慢慢侵蚀）形象；costly 点出转行成本递增。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Of course, interest cannot pay rent by itself; a basic income that supports an independent life is the bottom line any job must meet.","note":"Of course 让步 + bottom line（底线）划清边界，观点落地。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, choose the work that makes you want to get up in the morning, as long as it can support your life.","note":"makes you want to get up in the morning 把「兴趣」说成画面，as long as 补回底线条件。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Interest builds the future; salary only fills the present.","note":"future / present 对仗收尾，金句式结尾，值得背。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["A high-paying job you dislike, or a loved job with a modest salary? This is the first hard choice many graduates must make. In my view, interest should come first for a first job, though salary can never be completely ignored.","A career lasts for decades, and interest is what keeps a person growing through those years. Someone who loves his work learns faster, works more willingly and is more likely to become truly good at it — and income usually follows ability in the end. Salary, by contrast, can be a trap. A boring but well-paid job slowly eats away a young person's energy and curiosity, and after a few years, changing direction becomes costly. Of course, interest cannot pay rent by itself; a basic income that supports an independent life is the bottom line any job must meet.","In conclusion, choose the work that makes you want to get up in the morning, as long as it can support your life. Interest builds the future; salary only fills the present."],"id":"car-m6","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: When choosing a first job, some graduates put salary first, while others follow their interest. Which factor do you think matters more? Write 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"选工作看薪水还是看兴趣","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Changing jobs used to be a rare and serious decision.","note":"used to be 对比今昔，现象类经典起手。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Today, however, many young employees leave a job within a year or two, and some move several times before the age of thirty.","note":"用时间和次数写具体，现象的规模感出来。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Frequent job-hopping has become a noticeable feature of the young generation.","note":"job-hopping（跳槽）是本题关键词；noticeable feature 点题。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"The reasons are mixed.","note":"短句定调：原因有好有坏，预告下文两面分析。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"On the one hand, young people today value personal growth and feelings more than their parents did.","note":"先讲合理的一面；value（重视）用词准，两代对比。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"If a job offers no future, low pay and an unhappy atmosphere, they see little reason to stay.","note":"三个名词并列列出离职理由，see little reason to do 句型好用。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The fast-developing economy also provides more choices than ever before.","note":"than ever before 补时代背景原因。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"On the other hand, some job-hopping is simply impatience.","note":"转折点出不合理的一面：impatience（没耐心）一词定性。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Real skills and trust take years to build in any field; leaving at the first difficulty means starting from zero again and again, and a resume full of short stays makes employers doubt a person's loyalty and patience.","note":"分号长句一路推演频繁跳槽的代价；loyalty（忠诚度）是雇主视角的关键词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, changing jobs is a right, but it should be a step upward, not an escape.","note":"a step upward / an escape 对比给跳槽定性，评论有判断。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Move for a clearer direction, not merely for a change.","note":"祈使句收尾：为方向而动，不为变动而动——好背的金句。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Changing jobs used to be a rare and serious decision. Today, however, many young employees leave a job within a year or two, and some move several times before the age of thirty. Frequent job-hopping has become a noticeable feature of the young generation.","The reasons are mixed. On the one hand, young people today value personal growth and feelings more than their parents did. If a job offers no future, low pay and an unhappy atmosphere, they see little reason to stay. The fast-developing economy also provides more choices than ever before. On the other hand, some job-hopping is simply impatience. Real skills and trust take years to build in any field; leaving at the first difficulty means starting from zero again and again, and a resume full of short stays makes employers doubt a person's loyalty and patience.","In my view, changing jobs is a right, but it should be a step upward, not an escape. Move for a clearer direction, not merely for a change."],"id":"car-m7","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many young employees change jobs frequently, some leaving within the first year. Analyze the reasons for this phenomenon and give your comments in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"年轻人频繁跳槽","type":"现象类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"Graduation forces every student from a small town to make a geographical choice: fight for a future in the big city, or return home?","note":"冒号 + 问句摆出两难，geographical choice 说法新颖。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Both choices have their own logic, and neither is right for everyone.","note":"先不定论，预告对比分析，对比类稳妥的开局。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Big cities offer what hometowns usually cannot: more job opportunities, higher salaries and a wider view of the world.","note":"what 主语从句 + 冒号三点并列，大城市的好处一句说全。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"A young person can meet excellent peers and grow quickly under pressure.","note":"peers（同龄人/同行）准词；under pressure 点出成长机制。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"However, the price is heavy — high rent, long commutes and fierce competition make life tiring, and being far from family can feel lonely in hard times.","note":"破折号列出三重代价；commutes（通勤）是城市话题准词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Hometowns offer the opposite: a lower cost of living, the warmth of family and friends, and a slower, calmer pace.","note":"the opposite 与前段对称，三点并列一一对应，结构工整。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Yet chances are fewer, and some young people may feel their ambitions slowly shrinking.","note":"ambitions shrinking（ ambition 变小）说法形象，家乡的短板点到为止。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"As for me, I would spend my first years in a big city while I am young and energetic, and keep the hometown as a warm choice for later.","note":"个人选择按人生阶段安排：先闯后归，两边都不否定。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"The best place is the one that fits the stage of your life.","note":"fits the stage of your life 收尾，结论有哲理且不鸡汤。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["Graduation forces every student from a small town to make a geographical choice: fight for a future in the big city, or return home? Both choices have their own logic, and neither is right for everyone.","Big cities offer what hometowns usually cannot: more job opportunities, higher salaries and a wider view of the world. A young person can meet excellent peers and grow quickly under pressure. However, the price is heavy — high rent, long commutes and fierce competition make life tiring, and being far from family can feel lonely in hard times. Hometowns offer the opposite: a lower cost of living, the warmth of family and friends, and a slower, calmer pace. Yet chances are fewer, and some young people may feel their ambitions slowly shrinking.","As for me, I would spend my first years in a big city while I am young and energetic, and keep the hometown as a warm choice for later. The best place is the one that fits the stage of your life."],"id":"car-m8","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: After graduation, some students stay in big cities to build their careers, while others return to their hometowns. Compare the two choices and state your preference in 120–180 words.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"留在大城市还是回家乡工作","type":"利弊类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"},{"analysis":[{"en":"When two graduates with similar grades apply for the same job, the one with internship experience usually wins.","note":"用一个对比场景开头，重要性不用论证就显出来了；internship（实习）是本题关键词。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In my view, internships are one of the most valuable things a college student can do before graduation.","note":"one of the most… 表态，语气肯定。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"To begin with, an internship turns classroom knowledge into real ability.","note":"理由一主题句：turn…into… 把转化说清。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"Only in a real company do students learn how work is organized, how teams cooperate and how problems are solved under time pressure.","note":"Only in…do students… 倒装 + 三个 how 并列，全篇最亮的句式。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Besides, internships help students discover their true direction.","note":"理由二换角度：从能力到方向。","tag":"好结构"},{"en":"A few weeks in a workplace can reveal whether a dream job fits them or not, saving years of wrong choices after graduation.","note":"reveal whether…（揭示是否适合）；saving years 分词补结果，实习的试错价值说透。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"Employers value internships for the same reason: a student who has worked before needs less training and carries less risk.","note":"换到雇主视角补一层论证；carry less risk（风险更低）说法专业。","tag":"好词"},{"en":"Admittedly, a poor internship spent making tea and copies teaches little, so choosing a position with real tasks matters greatly.","note":"Admittedly 让步：端茶复印的实习没用——让步带出「要选有真任务的实习」的洞察。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"In conclusion, an internship is a bridge between campus and society.","note":"bridge 比喻收尾定位。","tag":"好句"},{"en":"The earlier students cross it, the smoother their first steps into work will be.","note":"The earlier…, the smoother… 句式呼应 bridge，首尾成环。","tag":"好句"}],"essay":["When two graduates with similar grades apply for the same job, the one with internship experience usually wins. In my view, internships are one of the most valuable things a college student can do before graduation.","To begin with, an internship turns classroom knowledge into real ability. Only in a real company do students learn how work is organized, how teams cooperate and how problems are solved under time pressure. Besides, internships help students discover their true direction. A few weeks in a workplace can reveal whether a dream job fits them or not, saving years of wrong choices after graduation. Employers value internships for the same reason: a student who has worked before needs less training and carries less risk. Admittedly, a poor internship spent making tea and copies teaches little, so choosing a position with real tasks matters greatly.","In conclusion, an internship is a bridge between campus and society. The earlier students cross it, the smoother their first steps into work will be."],"id":"car-m9","kind":"mock","prompt":"Directions: Many employers prefer graduates with internship experience. Do you think internships are important for college students? Write 120–180 words to state your view.","source":"模拟题","suggestedMinutes":30,"themeId":"career","themeName":"职业规划","title":"实习经历对找工作有多重要","type":"观点类","wordRequirement":"120–180 词"}];
